WEBVTT

1
00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:44.800
It's small!

2
00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:00.690
No, please.  No!
Please!

3
00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:02.280
Davey!

4
00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:04.780
Come a runnin', lad!

5
00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:08.870
- Stop!
- Brand you like a damn steer!

6
00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:11.530
- Bitch!
- No.  Please!

7
00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.080
Hold the bitch, Davey!
Go on, hold her!

8
00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:17.710
Hold her, damn it,
or I'll cut her tits off!

9
00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:20.050
Go get Skinny!  Quick!

10
00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:22.760
Mike, don't!

11
00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:29.350
Skinny!

12
00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:31.270
You think it's funny?

13
00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:35.560
Skinny, get the gun!

14
00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.370
Get off of her, cowboy.

15
00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.630
- They wouldn't let you settle it, huh?
- Hell, you know how Skinny is.

16
00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:01.300
He says he's gonna shoot 'em.
I says, "Skinny, you can't do that."

17
00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.380
and he says, "Well let's get Little Bill
in here and settle this thing."

18
00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:04.980
and I says, "Little Bill's sleeping."

19
00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:08.890
He says, "He don't care."
In another five minutes he's gonna shoot them boys.

20
00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:23.870
She going to die?

21
00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.910
She's going to live.

22
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:30.920
She didn't steal nothing...
she didn't even touch his poke.

23
00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.840
All she done, when she seen
he had a teensy little pecker...

24
00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:36.720
...was give a giggle, that's all.
She didn't know no better.

25
00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:42.430
You can hang 'em, Little Bill.

26
00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.760
Clyde...

27
00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:05.960
step over to the office
and get the bullwhip.

28
00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:10.830
A whippin?  That's all they get
after what they done?

29
00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.300
- Whippin' ain't no little thing, Alice.
- But what they done they...

30
00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.550
Alice!  Shut up!

31
00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:24.140
- Little Bill... whippin' ain't going to settle this.
- Oh no?

32
00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:28.020
This here's a lawful contract between me
and Delilah Fitzgerald, the cut whore.

33
00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:34.110
I brought her clear from Boston,
paid her expenses and all.

34
00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:38.040
I got a contract that represents
an investment of capital.

35
00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:39.580
Property.

36
00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.620
Damaged property.

37
00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:45.460
Like if I was to hamstring
one of their cow ponies.

38
00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.090
Well you figure nobody'll wanna
fuck her now, right?

39
00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:52.460
Hell, no!

40
00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:54.510
Least ways won't pay to do it!

41
00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.860
Maybe she can clean up
the place or something,

42
00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:59.060
but nobody's going to pay
good money for a cut-up whore!

43
00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:06.940
You boys are off the Bar T.
You got your own string of ponies?

44
00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:09.690
Yeah, I got four.

45
00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:13.910
Six.

46
00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:18.160
Guess you'd just as soon
not have a trial, no fuss, huh?

47
00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.160
No, sir.

48
00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:22.210
All right.

49
00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:24.500
You did the cutting.

50
00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:28.340
Come the fall, you bring in five ponies
and you give them over to Skinny here.

51
00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.260
Five?

52
00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:33.310
And you!
You bring in two.

53
00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.680
- You give them over, you hear?
- Yes, sir.

54
00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:37.840
The bullwhip Bill.

55
00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:42.730
Maybe we don't need this whip now.

56
00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:48.860
Let me tell you, come the spring,
Skinny don't have those ponies...

57
00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:53.240
- I'm gonna come looking for you.
- You ain't even gonna whip 'em?

58
00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:57.490
Well I fined them instead, Alice.

59
00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:01.160
For what they done, Skinny gets
some ponies and that's it?!

60
00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:03.710
That ain't fair Little Bill.

61
00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:05.290
That ain't fair!

62
00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:15.020
Haven't you seen enough
blood for one night, hmm?

63
00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:20.440
Hell, Alice!

64
00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:26.090
It ain't like they was tramps
or loafers or bad men.

65
00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:27.520
You know, they were just...

66
00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:30.460
...hardworking boys that was foolish.

67
00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:33.370
If they was given over to wickedness
in a regular way I'd understand...

68
00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:34.570
Like whores?

69
00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:38.290
Alice!... Tend to Delilah.

70
00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:42.250
Go ahead.

71
00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:06.360
I got $85.

72
00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:08.080
I don't know.

73
00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:11.820
If Delilah doesn't care one way or the
other, what are we getting so riled up about?

74
00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:15.740
Just because we let them smelly
fools ride us like horses...

75
00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:19.210
...don't mean we gotta let
them brand us like horses.

76
00:07:19.630 --> 00:07:24.710
Maybe we ain't nothing but whores,
but we... by God, we ain't horses!

77
00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:28.670
I got $112.

78
00:07:29.850 --> 00:07:31.100
That's everything.

79
00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:32.850
How about you, Faith?

80
00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:37.190
200.

81
00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:41.610
$240.

82
00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:45.150
Jesus, Faith!
What you been doing?

83
00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:47.940
You been giving Skinny something special?

84
00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:54.630
She laughed.

85
00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:01.710
With what Kate got, and Silky got some,
and then mine and Little Sue...

86
00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:03.170
It ain't enough.

87
00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:06.890
Not yet, maybe.

88
00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:50.050
You don't look like no rootin'-tootin'...

89
00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:52.730
...son-of-a-bitching cold-blooded assassin.

90
00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:58.820
Say what?

91
00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:02.530
My guess is you're calling
yourself Mr. William Munny.

92
00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:07.210
You have me confused with
someone else, mister.

93
00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:10.750
The same one who shot Charlie Pepper
up in Lake County?

94
00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:13.030
Pa! Hey Pa!

95
00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:14.760
Yeah, what's up, son?

96
00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:17.000
Two more hogs got the fever.

97
00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:19.050
You shot Charlie Pepper didn't you?

98
00:09:19.310 --> 00:09:22.640
...and you're the one who killed William Harvey
and robbed that train over in Missouri.

99
00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:24.170
Now hold on, mister.

100
00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:28.100
Son, get those hogs separated there.

101
00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:30.230
Penny, why don't you help your brother out.

102
00:09:30.530 --> 00:09:32.730
That one's sick too.

103
00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.110
We'll talk inside.

104
00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:49.500
So you're Pete Sothow's nephew, huh?

105
00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:55.380
I thought maybe you was someone come to kill
me for something I'd done in the old days.

106
00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:58.430
I could have.

107
00:09:58.770 --> 00:09:59.800
Easy.

108
00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:04.310
I guess maybe so.

109
00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:10.770
Like I was sayin' you don't look like
no meaner-than-hell, cold-blooded, damn killer.

110
00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:13.310
Maybe I ain't.

111
00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:17.950
Yeah, well Uncle Pete says you was the
meanest goddamn son-of-a-bitch alive.

112
00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:20.610
And if I ever wanted a
partner for a killing...

113
00:10:21.210 --> 00:10:23.000
...you were the worst one.

114
00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:28.330
Meaning the best.

115
00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:31.290
On account as you're
as cold as the snow...

116
00:10:31.550 --> 00:10:34.420
...and you don't have
no weak nerve nor fear.

117
00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:38.720
Pete said that, huh?

118
00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:42.050
Yeah, he did.

119
00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:44.600
I'm a damn killer myself, except...

120
00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:48.060
...I ain't killed as many as
you because of my youth.

121
00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:50.810
Schofield Kid, that's what they call me.

122
00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:55.360
Why?

123
00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:57.860
You from Schofield?

124
00:10:58.250 --> 00:10:59.870
No, it's on account...

125
00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:03.570
...of my Schofield model
Smith & Wesson pistol.

126
00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:09.920
How about it, Will?

127
00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:12.510
How about what?

128
00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:15.180
How about being my partner?

129
00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:18.360
I'm heading up North in
through Niobrara up to Wyoming.

130
00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:21.260
Gonna kill a couple of no-good cowboys.

131
00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:24.230
For what?

132
00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:28.480
For cutting up a lady.
Cut up her face.

133
00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:31.530
Cut her eyes out,
cut her ears off.

134
00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:34.780
Hell, they even cut her teets.

135
00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:39.240
Jesus!

136
00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:42.410
$1,000 reward, Will.

137
00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.170
500 apiece.

138
00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:51.550
Pa... I can't move those damn pigs!

139
00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:56.180
Watch your cussing now, will you?
Do the best you can with it.

140
00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:59.520
Then go to the pump
and get cleaned up.  Come on.

141
00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:08.400
I ain't like that anymore, Kid.

142
00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:13.120
It was whiskey done it as
much as anything else.

143
00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.780
I ain't had a drop in over 10 years.

144
00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:19.950
My wife, she cured me of that.

145
00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:24.420
Cured me of drinking and wickedness.

146
00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:28.260
Well you don't look so prosperous.

147
00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:33.470
Hell, you could buy her a new
dress with your half.

148
00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:36.250
If we kill them two, you can buy
your wife one of them fancy...

149
00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:38.310
She's passed on.

150
00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:40.610
What?

151
00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:44.770
Been gone near 3 years now.

152
00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:53.410
Don't tell no one else
about the reward and all.

153
00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:55.910
I don't need other
gunmen trying to collect.

154
00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:58.670
We don't see no one out here.

155
00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:00.270
Yeah.

156
00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:03.050
Well if you was to change your mind,
might be you could catch me,

157
00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:06.950
I'll be riding due West to the Western
Trail heading North into Wyoming.

158
00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:14.430
Come on, let's separate those hogs.

159
00:13:44.370 --> 00:13:46.080
Pa... two of them others...

160
00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:48.840
I think they got the fever.

161
00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:48.860
Took you boys a while.

162
00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:53.450
A couple more days and I was
going to call on the sheriff.

163
00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:54.960
How about that?

164
00:14:55.210 --> 00:14:58.330
The river was all swelled up.
Couldn't cross it.

165
00:14:58.590 --> 00:15:01.380
I bet.  Sleepy,
get them horses on in the livery.

166
00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:04.260
Neil, take that one
over around the back.

167
00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:14.260
Ah, now here's a beauty.

168
00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:17.610
You got two of mine.
This here one ain't yours.

169
00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:19.610
Oh, we gonna see about that.

170
00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:23.700
Bastards!
Get out of town!

171
00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:28.120
You are very sick sons of bitches!

172
00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:34.250
Don't come back, butcher!

173
00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:35.960
This here pony...

174
00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:39.590
...I brung for the lady,
the one my partner cut.

175
00:15:51.610 --> 00:15:52.980
She's the best of the lot.

176
00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:00.070
Better than the ones I gave him.

177
00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:06.530
She can sell her or...

178
00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:08.830
...or do what she wants.

179
00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:17.290
A pony?  She ain't got no face left,
you're gonna give her a god-damned mangy pony?

180
00:16:18.050 --> 00:16:19.630
She ain't mangy ma'am!

181
00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:22.300
Get out of here!

182
00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:25.880
We don't need your goddamn charity!

183
00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:29.010
Get out of our town
and don't come back!

184
00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:33.030
Get out of our town!

185
00:17:45.730 --> 00:17:48.730
Did Pa use to kill folks?

186
00:18:57.270 --> 00:19:00.640
Penny, I could tell your Ma liked
those flowers I gave her.

187
00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:04.600
He ain't hardly a saddle horse no more, Pa.
He ain't used to the feel.

188
00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:07.860
You take care of your sister now, son...

189
00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:12.860
and you kill a few chickens if you have to,
and keep those hogs that got the fever separate.

190
00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:17.830
If you have any problem, you go see
Sally Two Trees at Ned Logan's.

191
00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:46.280
Ain't hardly been in the saddle
myself in a while.

192
00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:53.650
This old horse is getting even with me
for the sins of my youth.

193
00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:58.080
In my youth before I met
your dear departed Ma...

194
00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:01.920
...I used to be weak
and given to mistreating animals.

195
00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:11.720
This horse and
those hogs over there...

196
00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:17.720
...are getting even with me for
the cruelty that I inflicted.

197
00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:19.730
I used to be able to cuss...

198
00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:24.780
...and whip a horse like this, but your Ma,
rest her soul, showed me the error of my ways.

199
00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:27.830
I'll be back in a couple of weeks.

200
00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:32.950
You remember how the spirit of your
dear departed Ma watches over you.

201
00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:53.810
- Where'd you get that money?
- We ain't got any money!

202
00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:57.400
- You told them cowboys you had it!
- We was lying!

203
00:20:57.860 --> 00:20:59.520
Lying?

204
00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:02.700
What are you gonna do when
somebody comes to collect?

205
00:21:04.330 --> 00:21:07.740
You going to hump them
a thousand times?

206
00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:14.420
The kind of people who come after that thousand
won't tolerate you not having it!

207
00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:20.050
They won't just cut up your face a little!

208
00:21:24.310 --> 00:21:26.510
You stupid bitches.

209
00:21:27.230 --> 00:21:29.180
You stupid bitches!

210
00:21:41.620 --> 00:21:42.650
Shit!

211
00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:45.450
Damn it!  Jesus!

212
00:21:47.330 --> 00:21:48.660
Hit your finger, huh?

213
00:21:51.170 --> 00:21:52.710
Hello, Skinny.

214
00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:55.160
Damn, you snuck up on me.

215
00:21:55.880 --> 00:21:58.010
What do you think of her?

216
00:21:58.260 --> 00:22:00.800
Well, I heard you done the roof yourself.

217
00:22:01.050 --> 00:22:05.630
Roof?  Jesus, Skinny, I did practically
the whole damn thing myself.

218
00:22:05.890 --> 00:22:09.760
The Roberts boy he carried some
wood for me, but that's all.

219
00:22:10.020 --> 00:22:11.900
What is all that wood?

220
00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:13.540
Well that's for my porch.

221
00:22:13.690 --> 00:22:15.940
I'm building a porch
so I can sit of an evening...

222
00:22:16.200 --> 00:22:20.740
...and smoke my pipe and drink coffee
and watch the sunset.

223
00:22:23.660 --> 00:22:26.330
Well... Came all the way out here
just to take a look at her, huh?

224
00:22:26.580 --> 00:22:28.570
- Oh them whores!
- Yeah?

225
00:22:28.830 --> 00:22:33.000
Them whores have been humping them cowboys
who been in town the last 2 weeks.

226
00:22:34.590 --> 00:22:36.220
Shit, Skinny.

227
00:22:37.930 --> 00:22:40.850
You know... We got railroad barons.
We got cattle barons.

228
00:22:41.100 --> 00:22:43.340
You're gonna be the first billiard baron.

229
00:22:44.140 --> 00:22:48.090
Yeah, well, they been humping them and
telling every bowlegged one of them...

230
00:22:48.360 --> 00:22:51.360
...that, uh, they're paying $1,000
to whatever son-of-a-bitch...

231
00:22:51.610 --> 00:22:54.610
...kills the two boys
that cut up Delilah.

232
00:22:56.820 --> 00:23:01.070
Those cowboys are riding that beef
down to Kansas and Cheyenne?

233
00:23:09.090 --> 00:23:10.500
How long?  All week?

234
00:23:10.800 --> 00:23:13.250
Well I didn't hear nothing
till last night myself.

235
00:23:13.880 --> 00:23:17.550
Hell, the word's probably got
all the way to Texas by now.

236
00:23:18.680 --> 00:23:20.760
Shit, Bill, I guess nobody's gonna
come clear from Texas.

237
00:23:23.270 --> 00:23:25.060
You sure those whores got all that money?

238
00:23:25.560 --> 00:23:27.810
Well, you know how women can lie.

239
00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:30.810
Knock 'em around a little bit, ask 'em
where the money is, they ain't got none.

240
00:23:31.070 --> 00:23:35.360
But they could have squirreled away
that much the five of 'em.  Maybe.

241
00:23:38.450 --> 00:23:40.030
That much, huh?

242
00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:43.450
You could run off them two cowboys.

243
00:23:44.460 --> 00:23:46.370
I could run off them whores.

244
00:23:49.380 --> 00:23:52.300
Well, I guess they'll just up and
run anyhow, them two.

245
00:23:55.620 --> 00:23:58.550
Nope...
They'll stay out there at the Bar T.

246
00:23:59.310 --> 00:24:00.970
Close to their friends.

247
00:24:02.560 --> 00:24:05.650
Shit, could be nobody won't come at all.

248
00:24:08.150 --> 00:24:10.390
Well, gotta go.
I like your house.

249
00:24:44.940 --> 00:24:47.020
Well, I'll be...

250
00:24:48.240 --> 00:24:49.860
It's Will!

251
00:24:54.540 --> 00:24:55.460
Hey Will!

252
00:24:56.500 --> 00:24:59.950
Come on in the house out
of the sun.  Sally...

253
00:25:00.210 --> 00:25:02.120
...see to Will's horse.

254
00:25:02.250 --> 00:25:03.420
Sally.

255
00:25:07.300 --> 00:25:09.040
What you doing here Will?

256
00:25:09.640 --> 00:25:11.790
Just thought I'd drop in on you.

257
00:25:13.560 --> 00:25:16.130
Yeah, Will, we ain't bad men no more.

258
00:25:16.480 --> 00:25:18.140
Shit, we're farmers.

259
00:25:18.560 --> 00:25:23.350
Should be easy killing them,
supposing they don't go on down to Texas first.

260
00:25:24.820 --> 00:25:29.070
How long has it been since you fired a gun
at a man Will?  Nine, ten years?

261
00:25:31.240 --> 00:25:32.400
Eleven.

262
00:25:34.330 --> 00:25:35.570
Easy, huh?

263
00:25:36.580 --> 00:25:39.670
I don't know it was
all that easy even back then.

264
00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:42.160
And we were young and full of beans.

265
00:25:43.010 --> 00:25:45.080
Mean, if you was mad at them Will, I mean...

266
00:25:45.760 --> 00:25:48.460
...if they done you some wrong,
I could see shooting them.

267
00:25:49.140 --> 00:25:51.840
We done stuff for money before Ned.

268
00:25:55.390 --> 00:25:57.520
We thought we did.

269
00:25:57.770 --> 00:26:00.810
All right so what'd these fellows do?
Cheat at cards?

270
00:26:01.070 --> 00:26:04.600
Steal some strays?
Spit on a rich fellow?  What?

271
00:26:04.990 --> 00:26:06.400
Naw, they cut up a woman.

272
00:26:06.780 --> 00:26:08.060
What?

273
00:26:09.450 --> 00:26:14.660
Cut up her face, cut her eyes out,
cut her fingers off, cut her tits.

274
00:26:16.380 --> 00:26:18.620
Everything but her cunny,
I suppose.

275
00:26:20.550 --> 00:26:22.120
I'll be dogged.

276
00:26:26.640 --> 00:26:28.460
Well... guess they got it coming.

277
00:26:30.060 --> 00:26:31.550
Of course, you know Will...

278
00:26:32.810 --> 00:26:35.730
...if Claudia was alive,
you wouldn't be doing this.

279
00:26:46.160 --> 00:26:49.030
Don't suppose you'd mind looking in
on my youngsters next week?

280
00:26:49.290 --> 00:26:51.460
They got some hogs
they're trying to separate.

281
00:26:51.730 --> 00:26:53.890
Will?...

282
00:26:54.630 --> 00:26:55.990
How long you reckon you're gonna be?

283
00:26:58.750 --> 00:27:00.250
Two weeks, I guess.

284
00:27:03.270 --> 00:27:04.350
Will?...

285
00:27:09.570 --> 00:27:10.350
Um...

286
00:27:12.270 --> 00:27:13.850
This Kid, what's he like?

287
00:27:17.020 --> 00:27:18.300
Three ways?

288
00:27:20.360 --> 00:27:23.110
I see you still have that Spencer rifle, huh?

289
00:27:25.200 --> 00:27:28.570
Yeah... and I can still knock the
eye out of a bird flying too.

290
00:27:37.880 --> 00:27:39.420
Jesus, Will!

291
00:28:36.610 --> 00:28:38.600
He must be moving right along.

292
00:28:39.110 --> 00:28:41.780
We'll come across him
tomorrow, I reckon.

293
00:28:53.550 --> 00:28:55.460
Kind of got used to my bed.

294
00:28:55.720 --> 00:28:58.170
This ain't going to be like no home.

295
00:28:59.300 --> 00:29:02.050
Bed ain't the only thing I'm gonna
be missing, I tell ya.

296
00:29:07.600 --> 00:29:08.930
Hell, Will, I'm sorry.

297
00:29:09.560 --> 00:29:13.060
Don't fret it.
It ain't nothing.

298
00:29:15.400 --> 00:29:17.200
She don't like it much does she...

299
00:29:17.450 --> 00:29:19.190
...you riding off with me?

300
00:29:20.200 --> 00:29:22.030
Gave me the evil eye.

301
00:29:26.000 --> 00:29:28.240
You know, Sally's injun...

302
00:29:29.130 --> 00:29:31.290
...and injuns ain't over-friendly Will.

303
00:29:33.510 --> 00:29:34.920
I don't blame her.

304
00:29:36.340 --> 00:29:38.250
I ain't gonna hold it against her.

305
00:29:38.510 --> 00:29:40.420
She knew me back then.

306
00:29:41.020 --> 00:29:42.430
She knew what a...

307
00:29:43.020 --> 00:29:45.420
...no-good son-of-a-bitch I was.

308
00:29:47.270 --> 00:29:49.850
She just ain't allowing that I've changed.

309
00:29:50.690 --> 00:29:53.440
She don't realize I
ain't like that no more.

310
00:29:53.700 --> 00:29:56.020
- You know Will....
- I ain't the same, Ned.

311
00:29:57.530 --> 00:30:02.280
Claudia straightened me up.
Cleared me of drinking whiskey and all.

312
00:30:03.710 --> 00:30:05.410
Just cause we're going on this killing...

313
00:30:05.670 --> 00:30:08.750
...that don't mean I'm gonna go
back to being the way I was.

314
00:30:10.130 --> 00:30:11.790
Just need the money.

315
00:30:12.300 --> 00:30:14.620
Get a new start for them youngsters.

316
00:30:20.390 --> 00:30:22.720
Ned, you remember that drover
I shot through the mouth...

317
00:30:22.980 --> 00:30:25.550
...and his teeth came
out the back of his head?

318
00:30:28.900 --> 00:30:30.980
I think about him now and again.

319
00:30:34.160 --> 00:30:36.910
He didn't do anything
to deserve to get shot...

320
00:30:37.830 --> 00:30:40.580
...least nothing I could
remember when I sobered up.

321
00:30:45.920 --> 00:30:48.490
You was one crazy son-of-a-bitch Will.

322
00:30:51.760 --> 00:30:54.710
Yeah, no one liked me
and the boys all thought...

323
00:30:54.970 --> 00:30:57.430
...I was gonna shoot them
out of pure meanness.

324
00:31:00.020 --> 00:31:01.930
You ain't like that no more.

325
00:31:02.850 --> 00:31:05.010
Eagle, he hated my guts.

326
00:31:06.690 --> 00:31:09.270
Bonaparte didn't think too much of me either.

327
00:31:09.860 --> 00:31:11.610
Quincy neither, I reckon.

328
00:31:14.030 --> 00:31:17.030
Quincy used to just watch all the time...

329
00:31:18.460 --> 00:31:19.950
...scared.

330
00:31:21.120 --> 00:31:22.620
Well, like I said...

331
00:31:24.130 --> 00:31:26.040
...you ain't like that no more.

332
00:31:27.050 --> 00:31:28.380
That's right.

333
00:31:29.970 --> 00:31:31.880
I'm just a fellow now.

334
00:31:32.140 --> 00:31:34.970
I ain't no different than anyone else...

335
00:31:35.720 --> 00:31:36.970
...no more.

336
00:31:52.370 --> 00:31:57.360
All I wanna know is what son-of-a-bitch shot him is all?
Was it one of them John Bulls?

337
00:31:57.620 --> 00:32:02.120
Oh, no, sir.  I believe the would-be assassin
to be a gentleman of French ancestry.

338
00:32:02.380 --> 00:32:06.160
Or so it would seem. I don't wish to
give offense when I observe...

339
00:32:06.420 --> 00:32:10.340
...but the French are known
to be a race of assassins...

340
00:32:10.600 --> 00:32:12.590
...though they can't shoot worth a damn.

341
00:32:12.850 --> 00:32:16.510
Any Frenchmen in the present
company are excluded, of course.

342
00:32:16.770 --> 00:32:21.510
Says here a fellow by the name
of Guiteau. G-U-I-T--

343
00:32:21.770 --> 00:32:25.440
Sure as hell sounds
like a John Bull to me.

344
00:32:25.860 --> 00:32:31.490
Well sir, again, I don't wish to give offense
when I suggest that this country should select...

345
00:32:31.740 --> 00:32:36.040
...a king or even a queen,
rather than a President.

346
00:32:38.000 --> 00:32:40.920
One isn't that quick
to shoot a king or a queen.

347
00:32:41.170 --> 00:32:43.710
The majesty of royalty, you see.

348
00:32:46.800 --> 00:32:49.720
Well maybe you don't wish
to give offense, sir...

349
00:32:50.010 --> 00:32:52.140
...but you are giving it pretty thick.

350
00:32:52.560 --> 00:32:55.310
This country don't need no
queens whatsoever I reckon.

351
00:32:55.640 --> 00:32:58.310
- As a matter of fact when I heared about queens...
- Shut up, Joe.

352
00:32:58.560 --> 00:33:01.320
What the hell's wrong with you, Thirsty?
This dude son-of-a-bitch...

353
00:33:01.570 --> 00:33:04.440
Might be that this dude
here is English Bob.

354
00:33:05.450 --> 00:33:08.480
He's the one works for the
railroad shooting Chinamen.

355
00:33:08.740 --> 00:33:12.570
Might be he's waiting for some
crazy cowboy to touch his pistol...

356
00:33:12.830 --> 00:33:14.450
...so he can shoot him down.

357
00:33:26.260 --> 00:33:28.000
Is that a fact, mister?

358
00:33:29.010 --> 00:33:30.760
You English Bob?

359
00:33:33.440 --> 00:33:34.430
Pheasants.

360
00:33:36.860 --> 00:33:38.850
Let's shoot some pheasants.

361
00:33:39.110 --> 00:33:40.350
Ten shots.

362
00:33:40.690 --> 00:33:43.360
At, let's say, $1 a pheasant.

363
00:33:44.030 --> 00:33:47.200
I'll shoot for the Queen, and you...

364
00:33:47.620 --> 00:33:49.200
...for... well, whomever.

365
00:34:05.640 --> 00:34:07.630
That's eight for me and one for you.

366
00:34:07.890 --> 00:34:10.460
That comes to seven of your American dollars.

367
00:34:11.140 --> 00:34:13.140
Pretty damn good shooting...

368
00:34:13.730 --> 00:34:15.470
...for a John Bull.

369
00:34:15.980 --> 00:34:18.730
Well no doubt your aim was
affected by your grief...

370
00:34:21.150 --> 00:34:23.650
...over the injury to your President.

371
00:34:35.840 --> 00:34:39.920
Ah, it's the climate that does it.
That, and the infernal distances.

372
00:34:40.260 --> 00:34:41.250
Does what?

373
00:34:41.680 --> 00:34:44.760
Induces people to shoot
persons in high places.

374
00:34:45.680 --> 00:34:46.960
Yeah, uh...

375
00:34:47.180 --> 00:34:49.290
You know it's a savage country really.

376
00:34:49.380 --> 00:34:52.560
That's the second one they've
shot in twenty years.

377
00:34:53.110 --> 00:34:56.810
It's uncivilized shooting
persons of substance.

378
00:35:53.760 --> 00:35:55.000
Thank you.

379
00:35:57.760 --> 00:35:59.170
Pardon me, gentlemen.

380
00:36:01.510 --> 00:36:04.140
The local ordinance obliges you
to surrender all sidearms...

381
00:36:04.210 --> 00:36:07.140
to the proper authorities for
the duration of your visit.

382
00:36:07.940 --> 00:36:09.220
Proper authority?

383
00:36:12.360 --> 00:36:14.280
Well I can assure you young man...

384
00:36:14.360 --> 00:36:17.780
that neither my companion
or I carry firearms on our person.

385
00:36:18.170 --> 00:36:21.250
We rely upon the goodwill
of our fellow man...

386
00:36:21.390 --> 00:36:24.670
...and the forbearance of reptiles.

387
00:36:38.300 --> 00:36:40.050
Unarmed, my ass!

388
00:36:41.270 --> 00:36:42.510
Oh, Christ, it's hot!

389
00:36:42.770 --> 00:36:47.350
If I'm going to get shot,
I'd rather it was hot than cold.

390
00:36:47.610 --> 00:36:49.730
Everything hurts me more when it's cold.

391
00:36:49.910 --> 00:36:52.030
You know how if you hit
your thumb and it's cold...

392
00:36:52.190 --> 00:36:53.380
Shut up, Fatty!

393
00:36:54.590 --> 00:36:55.400
I only said...

394
00:36:55.500 --> 00:36:57.000
Clyde's back.

395
00:36:57.080 --> 00:36:58.900
- Is  Little Bill with him?
- No.

396
00:36:59.700 --> 00:37:00.730
Shit!

397
00:37:06.170 --> 00:37:08.960
- You boys clean my Remington?
- Cleaned and loaded.

398
00:37:10.130 --> 00:37:12.000
Where's Little Bill for Christ's sake?

399
00:37:12.510 --> 00:37:14.130
Building his damn porch.

400
00:37:14.550 --> 00:37:16.210
Building his porch?

401
00:37:16.760 --> 00:37:20.130
If you gonna get shot Andy, would you
like it better on a hot day or a cold day?

402
00:37:20.430 --> 00:37:22.140
I ain't going to get shot.

403
00:37:24.100 --> 00:37:25.420
He's coming ain't he?

404
00:37:26.110 --> 00:37:28.020
Of course he's coming.

405
00:37:28.820 --> 00:37:30.230
I just loaded that, what you doing?

406
00:37:30.490 --> 00:37:33.520
I don't trust nobody to load
my guns for shooting.

407
00:37:35.120 --> 00:37:36.030
What'd he say?

408
00:37:36.490 --> 00:37:39.530
Little Bill?  Didn't say nothing.
He said he was building his porch.

409
00:37:40.330 --> 00:37:43.120
- You seen that thing?
- It was all loaded.

410
00:37:43.350 --> 00:37:47.440
Jesus, Clyde, you got three pistols
and you only got one arm for Christ's sake!

411
00:37:47.560 --> 00:37:50.420
I just don't want to get killed
for lack of shooting back.

412
00:37:53.260 --> 00:37:56.260
You know he don't have a straight
angle on that whole goddamn porch!

413
00:37:56.770 --> 00:37:58.760
Or the whole house, for that matter!

414
00:37:59.140 --> 00:38:01.270
He is the worst damn carpenter.

415
00:38:01.980 --> 00:38:03.600
He didn't say nothing, huh?

416
00:38:04.480 --> 00:38:06.390
Asked what they looked
like, that's all.

417
00:38:08.030 --> 00:38:10.780
Christ maybe he's tough but he
sure ain't no carpenter.

418
00:38:11.280 --> 00:38:13.070
Maybe he ain't so tough.

419
00:38:14.280 --> 00:38:15.940
Seem like he was scared?

420
00:38:17.870 --> 00:38:19.910
Little Bill?  Him scared?

421
00:38:21.210 --> 00:38:24.410
We never seen him up
against any like these ones.

422
00:38:24.710 --> 00:38:25.630
Killers.

423
00:38:27.050 --> 00:38:30.130
Little Bill come out of
Kansas and Texas, boys.

424
00:38:30.890 --> 00:38:32.930
He worked them tough towns.

425
00:38:33.260 --> 00:38:34.590
Just wondered.

426
00:38:36.600 --> 00:38:38.470
Anybody could be scared.

427
00:38:43.570 --> 00:38:45.480
Well, he wasn't scared, boys.

428
00:38:46.740 --> 00:38:48.480
He just ain't no carpenter.

429
00:38:54.450 --> 00:38:56.540
Well there's a dignity in royalty...

430
00:38:56.640 --> 00:39:00.120
...a majesty which precludes
the likelihood of assassination.

431
00:39:00.380 --> 00:39:01.920
Now if you were to point a pistol...

432
00:39:02.170 --> 00:39:05.460
...at a king or a queen,
your hands would shake as though palsied.

433
00:39:05.720 --> 00:39:08.560
I wouldn't point no pistol at nobody sir.

434
00:39:09.330 --> 00:39:11.640
Well that's a wise policy...
a wise policy...

435
00:39:12.260 --> 00:39:16.160
but if you did, I can assure you, if you did,
that the sight of royalty...

436
00:39:16.220 --> 00:39:20.730
...would cause you to dismiss all thoughts
of bloodshed and you would stand...

437
00:39:20.980 --> 00:39:22.390
...how should I put it...

438
00:39:22.650 --> 00:39:24.310
...in awe.

439
00:39:26.570 --> 00:39:32.030
Now... a President... well,
I mean... why not shoot a President?

440
00:39:37.790 --> 00:39:39.200
Keep the change.

441
00:39:39.460 --> 00:39:43.210
This Strawberry Alice
person, tell me again.

442
00:39:43.470 --> 00:39:47.210
Down the street and across...
Greely's Beer Garden and Billiard Parlor.

443
00:39:47.590 --> 00:39:50.000
Just ask for Alice, say you
want a game of billiards.

444
00:39:50.260 --> 00:39:53.550
Billiards?
Even though I don't really wish to play?

445
00:39:53.850 --> 00:39:57.220
No matter. They burned the
table in '78 for firewood.

446
00:39:58.310 --> 00:39:59.890
Quite right... quite right.

447
00:40:01.190 --> 00:40:03.860
Well Mr. Beauchamp,
I think a cup of tea...

448
00:40:18.960 --> 00:40:20.210
Hello, Bob.

449
00:40:22.880 --> 00:40:25.370
Boys, this here is English Bob.

450
00:40:26.890 --> 00:40:28.800
Shit and fried eggs!

451
00:40:31.390 --> 00:40:32.890
Been a long time Bob.

452
00:40:34.230 --> 00:40:35.640
Did you run out of Chinamen?

453
00:40:36.360 --> 00:40:37.570
Little Bill?

454
00:40:37.860 --> 00:40:40.670
Well, I thought that you was um...
well I thought that you were dead.

455
00:40:41.400 --> 00:40:43.810
I see you've shaved
your chin whiskers off.

456
00:40:44.780 --> 00:40:47.820
I was tasting the soup
two hours after I ate it.

457
00:40:48.870 --> 00:40:50.740
Well actually, what I heard was that you...

458
00:40:51.000 --> 00:40:53.780
...fell off your horse, drunk, of course...

459
00:40:54.080 --> 00:40:56.660
...and that you broke your bloody neck.

460
00:40:58.210 --> 00:41:00.170
I heard that one myself, Bob.

461
00:41:00.510 --> 00:41:02.420
Hell, I even thought I was dead.

462
00:41:02.720 --> 00:41:05.290
Till I found out it was just
that I was in Nebraska.

463
00:41:06.930 --> 00:41:08.010
Who's your friend?

464
00:41:08.770 --> 00:41:10.010
W. W. Beauchamp.

465
00:41:11.270 --> 00:41:13.840
This is Little Bill Daggett.

466
00:41:14.770 --> 00:41:16.810
And friends, of course.

467
00:41:17.200 --> 00:41:20.360
Daggett?  From Newton, Hays?  From Abilene?

468
00:41:21.110 --> 00:41:22.860
In person.

469
00:41:24.240 --> 00:41:26.530
You work for the railroads
too Mr. Beauchamp?

470
00:41:27.220 --> 00:41:30.100
No.... I write.  I write...

471
00:41:30.790 --> 00:41:31.820
Letters?

472
00:41:32.290 --> 00:41:34.040
Books, Bill.  Books.

473
00:41:35.130 --> 00:41:36.210
Actually...

474
00:41:36.800 --> 00:41:38.710
...he's my biographer.

475
00:41:44.970 --> 00:41:47.380
I wouldn't do that if I were you...

476
00:41:47.670 --> 00:41:49.180
Mr. Beauchamp.

477
00:41:55.280 --> 00:41:56.730
It's only a book.

478
00:41:57.320 --> 00:41:58.350
A book, huh?

479
00:42:04.640 --> 00:42:06.890
Well I guess that means you boys can read.

480
00:42:07.330 --> 00:42:13.200
So I guess that means you saw the signs outside
of town there saying surrender your firearms.

481
00:42:15.300 --> 00:42:17.210
But like you told young Andy here...

482
00:42:19.090 --> 00:42:20.720
...you're not armed, are you Bob?

483
00:42:22.350 --> 00:42:23.920
Well, not really, Bill.

484
00:42:25.310 --> 00:42:28.930
Got a Peacemaker, but that
wouldn't worry you, would it?

485
00:42:29.310 --> 00:42:33.160
I mean if you don't see it.
Or most particularly, if you don't hear it.

486
00:42:34.030 --> 00:42:35.730
I'm afraid so, Bob.

487
00:42:36.530 --> 00:42:38.400
I don't like firearms around.

488
00:43:00.510 --> 00:43:02.310
Be very careful with it, sonny.

489
00:43:06.730 --> 00:43:08.170
Charley...

490
00:43:08.730 --> 00:43:11.570
see what kind of books
Mr. Beauchamp is packing here.

491
00:43:16.240 --> 00:43:18.150
Make sure you don't get wet.

492
00:43:25.170 --> 00:43:26.410
No shit Lttle Bill...

493
00:43:26.670 --> 00:43:29.580
all he's got here is writing
stuff and this here book.

494
00:43:32.340 --> 00:43:34.420
"The Duck of Death"?

495
00:43:34.680 --> 00:43:35.960
Duke.

496
00:43:37.720 --> 00:43:39.130
"The Duke", Bill.

497
00:43:42.310 --> 00:43:44.300
Well, good afternoon, gentlemen.

498
00:43:44.560 --> 00:43:46.690
I'll have that .32, Bob.

499
00:43:59.830 --> 00:44:01.490
Now, Little Bill...

500
00:44:02.210 --> 00:44:05.490
...you will leave me at
the mercy of my enemies.

501
00:44:10.260 --> 00:44:12.100
Enemies, Bob?

502
00:44:14.890 --> 00:44:17.670
You been talking about the Queen again?

503
00:44:18.720 --> 00:44:19.970
On Independence Day?

504
00:44:33.070 --> 00:44:34.820
I guess you think I'm kicking you, Bob.

505
00:44:36.540 --> 00:44:37.990
But it ain't so!

506
00:44:38.410 --> 00:44:40.290
What I'm doing is talking!

507
00:44:40.580 --> 00:44:41.490
You hear?!

508
00:44:42.080 --> 00:44:44.410
Talking to all those villains
down there in Kansas!

509
00:44:44.670 --> 00:44:47.160
And I'm talking to all those
villains in Missouri!

510
00:44:54.930 --> 00:44:56.180
And all those villains...

511
00:44:57.600 --> 00:44:59.470
...down in Cheyenne!

512
00:45:05.280 --> 00:45:07.810
And I'm telling 'em there
ain't no whore's gold!

513
00:45:13.450 --> 00:45:16.490
And even if there was, well they
wouldn't want to come looking for it...

514
00:45:17.660 --> 00:45:18.860
...anyhow!

515
00:45:48.110 --> 00:45:49.570
What are you all looking at?!

516
00:45:49.820 --> 00:45:51.670
Go on! Get outta here!

517
00:45:52.120 --> 00:45:53.370
Scoot!

518
00:45:58.500 --> 00:46:00.410
Go on, mind your own business!

519
00:46:26.950 --> 00:46:28.630
Hey, Will?

520
00:46:29.450 --> 00:46:30.830
You ever go into town?

521
00:46:32.080 --> 00:46:35.950
On occasion.
To sell a hog, pick up supplies.

522
00:46:37.540 --> 00:46:39.830
No, no... I mean, get yourself a woman.

523
00:46:43.130 --> 00:46:45.340
No, I never go into town for that.

524
00:46:45.590 --> 00:46:47.470
A man like me?

525
00:46:48.510 --> 00:46:52.100
Only woman a man like me could get
is one he'd have to pay for.

526
00:46:52.770 --> 00:46:55.010
That ain't right, buying flesh.

527
00:46:56.610 --> 00:47:00.100
Claudia, rest her soul, would never
want me doing something like that...

528
00:47:00.360 --> 00:47:01.820
...me being a father and all.

529
00:47:05.870 --> 00:47:08.410
So.... you just use your hand?

530
00:47:14.420 --> 00:47:17.040
I don't miss it all that much.

531
00:47:34.460 --> 00:47:36.020
Will?!

532
00:47:37.860 --> 00:47:40.020
Goddamn!
Somebody's shooting at us!

533
00:47:41.360 --> 00:47:42.860
Did he hit you?

534
00:47:44.620 --> 00:47:47.650
Oh... no, I bumped my head
falling off my horse.

535
00:47:52.960 --> 00:47:54.870
Ain't shooting at us no more.

536
00:47:57.300 --> 00:47:58.870
Shooting way over yonder.

537
00:48:01.300 --> 00:48:03.380
What the hell's he shooting at over there?

538
00:48:03.970 --> 00:48:05.710
Beats the hell out of me.

539
00:48:08.890 --> 00:48:11.050
Don't reckon we in
somebody's field, do you?

540
00:48:11.310 --> 00:48:13.220
I didn't see nothing planted.

541
00:48:14.270 --> 00:48:15.730
Shooting at us again.

542
00:48:20.280 --> 00:48:22.690
Hell, he's shooting up
the whole horizon, Will.

543
00:48:23.910 --> 00:48:25.570
Wait!  You'll mark us!

544
00:48:25.830 --> 00:48:27.070
Hey, Kid!

545
00:48:29.020 --> 00:48:31.080
Kid?!...  You mean that's the Kid shooting at us?

546
00:48:31.420 --> 00:48:33.080
Hey Kid, it's me!  Will Munny!

547
00:48:33.340 --> 00:48:35.660
What the hell's the Kid shooting at us for?

548
00:48:35.920 --> 00:48:37.080
Is that you?

549
00:48:39.930 --> 00:48:41.250
Yeah... yeah, it's me!

550
00:48:41.800 --> 00:48:44.920
Now don't go shooting at us
no more!  You hear me?

551
00:48:45.680 --> 00:48:47.920
Who in the hell you got with you, Will?

552
00:48:49.020 --> 00:48:51.340
It's Ned Logan, my old partner!

553
00:48:51.690 --> 00:48:54.100
Now don't go shooting at us, you hear?

554
00:48:54.940 --> 00:48:57.780
We're gonna collect our horses
and come on over there.

555
00:48:58.150 --> 00:49:00.230
You ain't going to shoot, now are you?

556
00:49:02.130 --> 00:49:03.780
No... no, I ain't!

557
00:49:16.550 --> 00:49:20.680
- Chased that horse a damn mile.
- What the hell was you shooting at us for anyhow?

558
00:49:20.930 --> 00:49:23.680
- I thought you was following me.
- We was following you.

559
00:49:23.930 --> 00:49:28.430
- Like you said if I changed my mind...
- Wasn't nothing said about no partner, Will.

560
00:49:29.150 --> 00:49:30.970
Well, this here's Ned Logan.

561
00:49:31.230 --> 00:49:34.350
This is the Schofield Kid,
nephew to Pete Sothow.

562
00:49:34.610 --> 00:49:38.560
I seen two fellows following me.
My guess is you come to kill me.

563
00:49:40.080 --> 00:49:42.570
We never talked about no other fellow.

564
00:49:42.830 --> 00:49:47.210
Well, there's two of them cowboys isn't there?
Better there's three of us, in case they got friends.

565
00:49:47.460 --> 00:49:51.290
I figure I can take care of them two
cowboys myself.  It don't take three.

566
00:49:52.130 --> 00:49:56.380
Ned's an awful good shot with a rifle.
Hit a bird in the eye flying.

567
00:49:56.970 --> 00:49:58.840
Better than you, anyhow Kid.

568
00:49:59.350 --> 00:50:00.630
Hell, you wasn't even coming close.

569
00:50:00.890 --> 00:50:03.380
Get your damn hands off my rifle, mister!

570
00:50:12.780 --> 00:50:16.560
Thought I'd check it for you.
Thought maybe something was bent.

571
00:50:16.820 --> 00:50:18.230
It ain't bent.

572
00:50:19.370 --> 00:50:21.240
Well you were shooting all over creation!

573
00:50:21.500 --> 00:50:23.070
You gonna share your half with him?

574
00:50:23.750 --> 00:50:25.460
I figure three ways.

575
00:50:26.670 --> 00:50:28.040
You figured wrong.

576
00:50:29.710 --> 00:50:32.170
Sorry I wasted your time, Ned.

577
00:50:34.590 --> 00:50:36.300
What?  You going back with him?

578
00:50:37.350 --> 00:50:39.220
Well he's my partner.

579
00:50:39.560 --> 00:50:41.300
He don't go, I don't go.

580
00:50:46.060 --> 00:50:48.270
What's it come to, three ways?

581
00:51:42.290 --> 00:51:43.490
Shit!

582
00:51:45.130 --> 00:51:47.210
What the hell you pissing on about?

583
00:51:49.300 --> 00:51:52.880
- What are you looking at, anyhow?
- "Looking at"?

584
00:51:53.140 --> 00:51:54.510
Clouds, Kid.

585
00:51:54.930 --> 00:51:58.760
Looking at them clouds over yonder on
account of we got a storm riding up our ass.

586
00:52:00.940 --> 00:52:03.480
Oh, them?
Hell, I seen them.

587
00:52:13.950 --> 00:52:16.360
You was smart to change your mind, Kid.

588
00:52:19.630 --> 00:52:21.870
I'm a real good shot with this rifle.

589
00:52:24.510 --> 00:52:26.050
See that hawk up there?

590
00:52:29.470 --> 00:52:31.390
I could hit that hawk with one shot.

591
00:52:35.140 --> 00:52:39.060
Hell, l could hit it too, Ned.
If I didn't mind wasting a shot.

592
00:52:41.860 --> 00:52:43.570
There ain't no hawk, Kid.

593
00:52:44.650 --> 00:52:46.560
You can't see for shit, can you?

594
00:52:49.870 --> 00:52:51.570
See your canteen?

595
00:52:58.130 --> 00:52:59.540
Alright, how far can you see?

596
00:52:59.700 --> 00:53:00.780
Far enough.

597
00:53:00.990 --> 00:53:03.380
We ain't going to Wyoming to shoot
canteens goddamn it!  How far?

598
00:53:03.630 --> 00:53:05.870
- 100 yards?
- More.

599
00:53:06.130 --> 00:53:08.800
- Can you see that scrub oak yonder?
- Fuck you Ned.

600
00:53:09.050 --> 00:53:10.330
He's blind Will!

601
00:53:10.430 --> 00:53:12.090
I ain't blind you asshole!

602
00:53:12.520 --> 00:53:13.930
Now hold on!  Hold it!

603
00:53:14.810 --> 00:53:17.300
How far can you see, Kid?
50 yards?

604
00:53:17.810 --> 00:53:20.650
You bet your ass
I can see 50 yards, Will.

605
00:53:21.070 --> 00:53:24.640
I can see well enough to shoot this
son-of-a-bitch right here in front of me.

606
00:53:24.740 --> 00:53:26.280
Now hold on.

607
00:53:26.530 --> 00:53:27.940
You hear that, Ned?

608
00:53:28.240 --> 00:53:30.650
Kid can see 50 yards.  Fine.

609
00:53:31.950 --> 00:53:32.950
Jesus!

610
00:53:36.380 --> 00:53:39.740
50 yards'll do just fine.
Now let's move out.

611
00:53:49.140 --> 00:53:51.930
Boy, they look like real hard cases, Bob.

612
00:53:53.390 --> 00:53:54.970
Did you kill all seven of 'em dead?

613
00:53:55.230 --> 00:53:57.220
Or did you just wing some of 'em?

614
00:54:03.110 --> 00:54:06.320
Now that is you there embalmed on the cover?

615
00:54:08.620 --> 00:54:10.410
"The Duck of Death"?

616
00:54:11.830 --> 00:54:14.700
It's the Duke.
"Duke of Death."

617
00:54:18.630 --> 00:54:22.790
You always were hell in Jesus with
a pistol Bob, but seven of 'em?  Boy!

618
00:54:23.050 --> 00:54:25.820
And you protecting that woman and all that.
How in the hell do you do that?

619
00:54:29.160 --> 00:54:34.100
Well, you see, it's generally considered desirable
in the publishing business to take a certain...

620
00:54:34.360 --> 00:54:37.230
...liberty when you're
depicting the cover scene.

621
00:54:37.480 --> 00:54:39.310
It's for reasons involving the marketplace, etc....

622
00:54:39.610 --> 00:54:44.070
Well, Mr. Beauchamp, from what I read, this here book
the writing's not that much different than the picture.

623
00:54:46.410 --> 00:54:48.820
Well I can assure you, Mr. Daggett...

624
00:54:49.210 --> 00:54:52.910
...that the events that are described in there
are taken from the account of eyewitnesses, sir.

625
00:54:53.170 --> 00:54:54.230
Eyewitnesses?

626
00:54:54.370 --> 00:54:55.530
Yes sir!

627
00:54:56.000 --> 00:54:57.700
You mean like the Duck himself, I guess.

628
00:55:00.010 --> 00:55:01.210
The Duke.

629
00:55:01.640 --> 00:55:02.920
Duck, I says.

630
00:55:11.520 --> 00:55:15.570
"You have insulted the honor of
this beautiful woman, Corcoran..."

631
00:55:15.820 --> 00:55:17.060
...said the Duck.

632
00:55:18.400 --> 00:55:20.310
"You must apologize."

633
00:55:20.700 --> 00:55:23.150
"But Two-Gun Corcoran
would have none of it..."

634
00:55:23.410 --> 00:55:26.830
"and cursing, he reached for his
pistols and would have killed him...

635
00:55:27.080 --> 00:55:31.660
...but the Duck was faster and hot lead
blazed from his smoking six-guns."

636
00:55:33.210 --> 00:55:36.000
See I consider that to be an
accurate depiction of the events.

637
00:55:36.260 --> 00:55:40.630
Albeit, there is a certain poetry to the
language which I couldn't resist.

638
00:55:40.850 --> 00:55:42.520
Ahh, Mr. Beauchamp...

639
00:55:43.850 --> 00:55:47.020
I was in the Blue Bottle
Saloon in Wichita...

640
00:55:47.350 --> 00:55:50.350
...the night that English Bob
killed Corky Corcoran...

641
00:55:51.060 --> 00:55:52.770
and I didn't see you there.

642
00:55:53.610 --> 00:55:55.100
Nor no woman.

643
00:55:55.360 --> 00:55:57.480
No two-gun shooters.

644
00:55:57.780 --> 00:56:00.490
- Nor none of this.
- You were there?

645
00:56:00.740 --> 00:56:02.150
Yeah, I was there.

646
00:56:04.870 --> 00:56:06.200
First off...

647
00:56:06.870 --> 00:56:10.490
...Corky never carried two guns,
though he should have.

648
00:56:10.960 --> 00:56:12.870
He was called Two-Gun Corcoran.

649
00:56:13.130 --> 00:56:17.670
Yeah, well, a lot of folks did call him Two-Gun,
but that wasn't because he was sporting two pistols.

650
00:56:17.930 --> 00:56:19.920
It was because he had dick
that was so big...

651
00:56:20.180 --> 00:56:23.600
...it was longer than the barrel
on that Walker Colt that he carried.

652
00:56:24.690 --> 00:56:29.020
And the only the only insulting he ever did
was stick that thing of his into this French lady...

653
00:56:29.170 --> 00:56:30.850
...that English Bob here was kinda sweet on.

654
00:56:31.230 --> 00:56:36.650
You see the night that Corky walked into the Blue Bottle
and before he know's what's happening...

655
00:56:36.910 --> 00:56:40.410
...Bob here takes a shot at him!
And he misses 'cause he's so damn drunk.

656
00:56:40.660 --> 00:56:44.820
Now that bullet whizzing by panicked
old Corky... and he did the wrong thing.

657
00:56:45.670 --> 00:56:48.610
He went for his gun in such a hurry
he shot his own damn toe off.

658
00:56:48.920 --> 00:56:50.750
Meantime, Bob here...

659
00:56:51.670 --> 00:56:54.340
...he's aiming real good
and he squeezes off another...

660
00:56:54.590 --> 00:56:59.550
...but he misses, cause he's still so damn drunk
and he hits a $1,000 mirror over the bar.

661
00:57:00.120 --> 00:57:03.270
But now, the Duck of Death is as good as dead...

662
00:57:03.430 --> 00:57:05.550
...because Corky does it right.

663
00:57:06.230 --> 00:57:07.940
He aims real careful.

664
00:57:08.400 --> 00:57:10.190
- No hurry.
- And?

665
00:57:12.610 --> 00:57:18.070
That Walker Colt blew up in his hand,
which was a failing common to that model.

666
00:57:18.830 --> 00:57:22.990
You see if Corky had've had two guns
instead of just a big dick...

667
00:57:24.210 --> 00:57:26.880
he would've been there right
to the end to defend himself.

668
00:57:27.210 --> 00:57:28.590
Wait a minute, you mean...

669
00:57:29.630 --> 00:57:33.500
that English Bob killed him when
he didn't even have...

670
00:57:33.840 --> 00:57:37.430
Well old Bob wasn't going to wait
for Corky to grow a new hand.

671
00:57:37.850 --> 00:57:40.600
No, he just walked
over there real slow...

672
00:57:42.100 --> 00:57:43.350
...because he was drunk...

673
00:57:45.730 --> 00:57:47.770
...and shot him right through the liver.

674
00:58:08.210 --> 00:58:10.620
Damn I don't like rocks
on my dadgum back!

675
00:58:11.550 --> 00:58:15.500
- I sure do miss my bed.
- You said that last night.

676
00:58:15.600 --> 00:58:20.100
No, last night I said I missed my wife.
Tonight I just miss my dadgum bed!

677
00:58:21.400 --> 00:58:24.950
You'll miss your dadgum roof
here in a while, I suppose.

678
00:58:26.320 --> 00:58:27.730
Shit!

679
00:58:39.310 --> 00:58:41.070
- Say, Will?
- Um-hmm?

680
00:58:42.710 --> 00:58:44.870
That business up in Jackson County...

681
00:58:45.130 --> 00:58:46.840
...that really happen?

682
00:58:47.090 --> 00:58:48.800
I mean the way they say it happened?

683
00:58:49.720 --> 00:58:50.710
What business?

684
00:58:53.430 --> 00:58:57.260
On how there's two deputies up close
pointing their rifles right at you.

685
00:58:57.520 --> 00:58:59.260
Had you dead to rights.

686
00:58:59.600 --> 00:59:02.560
You pulled out your pistol
and blew them both to hell.

687
00:59:03.270 --> 00:59:05.020
Only took a scratch yourself.

688
00:59:11.780 --> 00:59:14.320
Uncle Pete says he never
seen nothing like it...

689
00:59:14.580 --> 00:59:17.120
...shooting your way out
of a scrape like that.

690
00:59:21.250 --> 00:59:23.460
Yeah...  well I don't recollect.

691
00:59:26.800 --> 00:59:28.630
You don't recollect?

692
00:59:29.470 --> 00:59:30.580
That's right.

693
00:59:32.510 --> 00:59:33.550
Say Ned...

694
00:59:36.770 --> 00:59:38.510
...how many men you killed?

695
00:59:43.320 --> 00:59:45.060
Aren't you going to answer the question?

696
00:59:45.650 --> 00:59:47.400
What the hell's that to you?

697
00:59:50.330 --> 00:59:55.120
Well I gotta know what kind of fellow I'm riding
with, in case we get into a scrape and all.

698
00:59:58.670 --> 01:00:00.630
How many men you killed, Kid?

699
01:00:01.250 --> 01:00:02.250
Five.

700
01:00:02.510 --> 01:00:03.500
How many?

701
01:00:06.300 --> 01:00:07.300
Five!

702
01:00:08.390 --> 01:00:10.460
I done killed five of them.

703
01:00:12.060 --> 01:00:15.840
That's including a Mexican.
He come after me with a knife.

704
01:00:16.100 --> 01:00:18.310
Why don't you shut up?
Get some rest.

705
01:00:19.690 --> 01:00:23.310
You boys are as crotchety as a
couple of old hens, let me tell ya.

706
01:00:25.700 --> 01:00:30.770
Actually, then, Mr. Corcoran was faster
on the draw than the Duck...

707
01:00:31.580 --> 01:00:32.820
Than English Bob?

708
01:00:33.080 --> 01:00:35.830
Faster?
Faster was his mistake.

709
01:00:36.080 --> 01:00:39.540
If he hadn't been in such a goddamned hurry, he wouldn't
have shot himself in the toe with that first shot.

710
01:00:39.800 --> 01:00:41.840
He would've killed old Bob.

711
01:00:42.700 --> 01:00:43.840
Look, son...

712
01:00:45.220 --> 01:00:48.260
Being a good shot,
being quick with a pistol...

713
01:00:48.510 --> 01:00:52.890
...that don't do no harm, but it don't
mean much next to being cool-headed.

714
01:00:53.560 --> 01:00:57.310
A man who'll keep his head,
not get rattled under fire...

715
01:00:57.900 --> 01:00:59.440
...like as not he'll kill you.

716
01:00:59.690 --> 01:01:04.440
- But if the other fellow is quicker and fires first...
- Then he'll be hurrying and he'll miss.

717
01:01:04.700 --> 01:01:06.070
Look here.

718
01:01:08.870 --> 01:01:14.080
That's about as fast as I can draw and aim
and hit anything more than 10 feet away.

719
01:01:14.460 --> 01:01:16.120
Unless it's a barn.

720
01:01:16.590 --> 01:01:18.500
But if he doesn't miss?

721
01:01:20.300 --> 01:01:21.540
Then he'll kill you.

722
01:01:25.850 --> 01:01:29.630
That's why there's so few
dangerous men around like old Bob.

723
01:01:30.440 --> 01:01:31.430
Like me.

724
01:01:32.490 --> 01:01:34.610
It ain't so easy to shoot
a man anyhow, you know

725
01:01:34.700 --> 01:01:36.410
especially if the son-of-a-bitch
is shooting back at you.

726
01:01:36.570 --> 01:01:38.720
I mean that'll just flat rattle some folks.

727
01:01:40.570 --> 01:01:42.530
Let me show you something.

728
01:01:42.820 --> 01:01:45.490
Look here.
Take that.

729
01:01:48.710 --> 01:01:50.250
Go on, take it.

730
01:01:54.630 --> 01:01:56.170
There's the key.

731
01:01:57.340 --> 01:01:58.940
All you gotta do is shoot me...

732
01:01:59.800 --> 01:02:03.620
...and you and Bob can just
ride on out of here free as birds.

733
01:02:08.940 --> 01:02:12.980
- Is it loaded?
- Wouldn't do much good if it wasn't.

734
01:02:13.230 --> 01:02:15.060
First, you got to cock it.

735
01:02:21.990 --> 01:02:23.530
Go on, cock it.

736
01:02:31.710 --> 01:02:33.370
Now you got to point it.

737
01:02:37.010 --> 01:02:38.500
Go on.  Point it.

738
01:02:47.980 --> 01:02:50.680
Now all you got to do
is pull the trigger, mister.

739
01:03:05.790 --> 01:03:07.410
Hot, ain't it?

740
01:03:09.130 --> 01:03:11.500
You didn't even put your
finger on the trigger.

741
01:03:12.710 --> 01:03:14.210
What if...

742
01:03:15.470 --> 01:03:16.880
What if I gave it to him?

743
01:03:18.550 --> 01:03:19.800
Give it to him.

744
01:03:27.850 --> 01:03:29.530
...wh... you don't really want me to...

745
01:03:29.630 --> 01:03:31.130
Give it to him.

746
01:04:32.470 --> 01:04:34.790
I guess he don't want it, Mr. Beauchamp.

747
01:04:56.660 --> 01:04:58.780
You were right not to take it, Bob.

748
01:04:59.040 --> 01:05:00.450
I would have killed you.

749
01:05:19.600 --> 01:05:21.640
We could use some rain, Mr. Beauchamp.

750
01:05:32.530 --> 01:05:35.020
You no-good, goddamn pig-fucking whore!

751
01:05:36.410 --> 01:05:38.400
Sorry, old horse.

752
01:05:49.640 --> 01:05:52.590
I brung this along for when
we have to kill them fellows.

753
01:05:52.850 --> 01:05:55.050
Figured we could use some now.

754
01:05:55.310 --> 01:05:57.550
Not me.  I don't touch it no more.

755
01:05:57.810 --> 01:06:00.980
- Aw, come on, Will, it's raining.
- I know it's raining!

756
01:06:01.230 --> 01:06:03.220
Give some to the Kid why don't you.

757
01:06:06.030 --> 01:06:08.700
You think that Kid
really killed five men?

758
01:06:10.200 --> 01:06:11.570
No.

759
01:06:15.580 --> 01:06:20.710
When you were talking back there about the time
them deputies had the drop on you and Pete...

760
01:06:23.760 --> 01:06:27.170
Well, I remember there was
three men you shot, Will, not two.

761
01:06:27.430 --> 01:06:29.830
Well I ain't like that no more, Ned!

762
01:06:30.140 --> 01:06:32.540
I ain't no crazy killing fool.

763
01:06:35.060 --> 01:06:38.590
Still think it's gonna be
easy to kill them cowboys?

764
01:06:39.270 --> 01:06:41.560
If we don't drown first.

765
01:06:50.660 --> 01:06:52.990
Give these keys to the conductor.

766
01:06:54.040 --> 01:06:57.870
Tell him he can loose old Bob's cuffs
as soon as he's outside the county.

767
01:06:58.790 --> 01:07:00.590
Got my pistols?

768
01:07:02.800 --> 01:07:04.870
I guess you know, Bob that, uh...

769
01:07:05.180 --> 01:07:08.680
...if I see you again I'm just gonna
start shooting and figure it's self-defense.

770
01:07:15.230 --> 01:07:17.390
I didn't steal your biographer!

771
01:07:20.110 --> 01:07:21.940
He's staying on his own account!

772
01:07:22.360 --> 01:07:25.320
Well he can go stuff himself
as well, can't he?!

773
01:07:25.570 --> 01:07:28.570
A plague on ya... a plague on
the whole stinking lot of ya!

774
01:07:28.870 --> 01:07:30.940
Without morals or laws!

775
01:07:31.710 --> 01:07:35.370
And all you whores!
You got no laws, you got no honor!

776
01:07:35.920 --> 01:07:39.370
I tell you for a fact it's no
wonder you all emigrated to America!

777
01:07:39.630 --> 01:07:42.470
Because they wouldn't have you in England!

778
01:07:43.380 --> 01:07:45.420
You're a lot of savages,
that's what you all are...

779
01:07:45.680 --> 01:07:49.510
...a bunch of bloody savages!
A curse on ya!

780
01:07:51.560 --> 01:07:54.020
Nobody's going to come...

781
01:07:54.400 --> 01:07:57.430
...after what Little Bill done
to that Englishman.

782
01:07:58.780 --> 01:08:02.190
Delilah, them tables ain't clean...
can't you get 'em clean?

783
01:08:02.660 --> 01:08:05.500
and maybe if you'd cover up your face,
somebody might wanna hump with you

784
01:08:05.560 --> 01:08:07.200
and you wouldn't have to do all that cleaning.

785
01:08:08.540 --> 01:08:10.690
What do they call them things
you cover up your face with?

786
01:08:10.940 --> 01:08:12.040
A veil.

787
01:08:12.290 --> 01:08:14.120
Yeah a veil.  Get a veil!

788
01:08:23.600 --> 01:08:25.340
Rain's coming.

789
01:08:26.140 --> 01:08:27.600
Thank God.

790
01:08:52.920 --> 01:08:54.330
You sure?

791
01:09:06.480 --> 01:09:08.020
You all right there, Will?

792
01:09:18.190 --> 01:09:20.280
Hey, 's a fellow asking for you Alice.

793
01:09:20.570 --> 01:09:22.950
Tonight?
You ain't joshing?

794
01:09:23.200 --> 01:09:25.190
This way, mister.

795
01:09:25.620 --> 01:09:28.540
Must be randy as hell
to come out in this shit.

796
01:09:38.720 --> 01:09:41.720
"No, no!  You're wrong,
Little Bill!" he said.

797
01:09:41.970 --> 01:09:45.260
"That's not a Curly J.
That's a Bobbed J!"

798
01:09:45.520 --> 01:09:48.390
He had changed it over.
And I said to him...

799
01:09:48.690 --> 01:09:51.720
..."Jim, you're a liar
and a horse thief!"

800
01:09:54.150 --> 01:09:58.100
Now when he saw the rest of 'em wasn't
gonna help him none, he started crying...

801
01:09:58.370 --> 01:10:00.940
...and sobbing and
just a carrying on.

802
01:10:01.200 --> 01:10:04.900
He said, "Oh, Bill please oh God,
please, don't kill me, Bill!"

803
01:10:05.160 --> 01:10:08.220
So I said, "Jim, it just makes me sick..."

804
01:10:08.960 --> 01:10:10.580
Open the window, will you?

805
01:10:11.090 --> 01:10:15.090
" ...to see a man carrying
two pistols and a Henry rifle...

806
01:10:15.590 --> 01:10:17.830
...and crying like a damn baby."

807
01:10:18.100 --> 01:10:20.300
- So you killed him?
- No.

808
01:10:20.850 --> 01:10:22.310
But I should have.

809
01:10:23.390 --> 01:10:25.270
I can't abide them kind.

810
01:10:25.560 --> 01:10:27.600
You see them in the taverns, you know.

811
01:10:27.900 --> 01:10:30.140
Tramps and drunk teamsters...

812
01:10:30.570 --> 01:10:32.480
and crazed miners.

813
01:10:33.240 --> 01:10:36.650
Sporting their pistols and
acting like they were bad men.

814
01:10:37.070 --> 01:10:41.020
But without any sand or character.
Not even any bad character.

815
01:10:44.540 --> 01:10:47.710
I do not like assassins...

816
01:10:48.460 --> 01:10:50.950
or men of low character.

817
01:10:52.300 --> 01:10:54.010
Like your friend, English Bob.

818
01:10:54.680 --> 01:10:56.670
But, now Bob, he was
no coward, you know.

819
01:10:56.930 --> 01:11:00.630
No, he wouldn't come up to your
face and cry and carry on like that--

820
01:11:01.520 --> 01:11:02.550
Sheriff... I just...

821
01:11:03.900 --> 01:11:06.520
Yeah, damn.  Well, I don't
have any more receptacles.

822
01:11:06.940 --> 01:11:08.930
Well, maybe you should
just hang the carpenter.

823
01:11:11.040 --> 01:11:12.530
What?

824
01:11:14.740 --> 01:11:17.860
I was just saying because of the...
You know, if you hang...

825
01:11:19.910 --> 01:11:21.190
Doesn't matter.

826
01:11:23.670 --> 01:11:25.460
What the hell?

827
01:11:26.040 --> 01:11:27.920
On a night like this!

828
01:11:29.260 --> 01:11:33.250
- Who in the hell is it?
- Deputy Charley Hecker, Bill.

829
01:11:35.040 --> 01:11:36.150
What?

830
01:11:36.850 --> 01:11:41.230
Three fellows just come into town, Bill.
They're down to Greely's.

831
01:11:41.480 --> 01:11:43.350
There's two of 'em got guns.

832
01:11:51.570 --> 01:11:54.150
What the hell's keeping that Kid?

833
01:11:55.830 --> 01:11:57.740
You don't suppose he's up...

834
01:11:59.080 --> 01:12:00.700
Jesus, Will!

835
01:12:01.040 --> 01:12:02.450
You look like shit.

836
01:12:07.090 --> 01:12:09.790
You remember Eagle Hendershot?

837
01:12:10.690 --> 01:12:11.790
Yeah.

838
01:12:14.390 --> 01:12:16.010
I saw him.

839
01:12:17.560 --> 01:12:18.930
Will, he's dead.

840
01:12:19.850 --> 01:12:21.680
No, I saw him, Ned.

841
01:12:22.520 --> 01:12:26.190
His head was all broke open.
You could see inside of it.

842
01:12:27.740 --> 01:12:30.690
Jesus!  Will.  You got a fever.

843
01:12:30.950 --> 01:12:34.280
- Take a drink, will you?
- Worms were coming out.

844
01:12:37.370 --> 01:12:40.490
Look, Will, I'm gonna go up
and see what's keeping the Kid.

845
01:12:40.790 --> 01:12:44.290
Must be he's getting an advance
from one of them sporting ladies.

846
01:12:46.350 --> 01:12:48.960
Will, uh... look, if I was to...

847
01:12:50.690 --> 01:12:55.110
I mean, if it worked out that I could
take a little time for myself...

848
01:12:55.290 --> 01:12:57.110
I don't suppose you would...

849
01:12:57.390 --> 01:12:58.970
I mean you wouldn't...

850
01:13:02.170 --> 01:13:04.640
Naw, I guess you wouldn't want to come.

851
01:14:27.100 --> 01:14:29.510
Give me the pistol, mister.

852
01:14:35.210 --> 01:14:37.120
I says give me over your pistol.

853
01:14:40.880 --> 01:14:42.260
I ain't drunk.

854
01:14:44.510 --> 01:14:48.330
Ordinance says you got to turn in
your firearms to the county office...

855
01:14:48.820 --> 01:14:50.360
...day or night.

856
01:14:57.190 --> 01:15:00.440
I guess you didn't see the sign,
what, with the weather and all, huh?.

857
01:15:02.530 --> 01:15:03.610
No.

858
01:15:04.950 --> 01:15:06.490
But I ain't...

859
01:15:07.240 --> 01:15:08.740
I ain't armed.

860
01:15:09.540 --> 01:15:12.990
What about your friends upstairs there?
They got any pistols?

861
01:15:16.260 --> 01:15:20.050
No, I guess...
no, they ain't armed either.

862
01:15:21.970 --> 01:15:23.510
Spilled your whiskey.

863
01:15:24.170 --> 01:15:25.510
Look, I said I...

864
01:15:25.560 --> 01:15:26.970
What's your name?

865
01:15:28.890 --> 01:15:30.140
William...

866
01:15:32.860 --> 01:15:34.020
...Hendershot.

867
01:15:37.780 --> 01:15:40.190
Well, Mr. William Hendershot...

868
01:15:42.280 --> 01:15:46.450
...what if I was to say you was a
no-good son-of-a-bitch and a liar?

869
01:15:49.040 --> 01:15:53.200
And then if I was to say that you shit in
your pants because of a cowardly soul...

870
01:15:54.340 --> 01:15:57.810
...I bet you'd show me that pistol right
quick wouldn't you, you'd shoot me dead.

871
01:15:57.970 --> 01:15:59.540
Isn't that so?

872
01:16:06.270 --> 01:16:08.430
Maybe, I guess.

873
01:16:10.150 --> 01:16:11.560
But the fact...

874
01:16:12.110 --> 01:16:15.310
...is I ain't carrying no firearm.

875
01:16:15.740 --> 01:16:17.020
Get up.

876
01:16:39.040 --> 01:16:40.120
Come on.

877
01:16:49.980 --> 01:16:52.220
What's this for, snakes and such?

878
01:16:52.740 --> 01:16:54.020
Yeah.

879
01:16:54.570 --> 01:16:57.610
We don't have any snakes in here,
Mr. Hendershot.

880
01:17:02.790 --> 01:17:07.080
It ain't loaded or...
Powder's wet?

881
01:17:10.380 --> 01:17:11.960
You see, Mr. Beauchamp?

882
01:17:15.090 --> 01:17:17.580
This is the kind of
trash I was speaking of!

883
01:17:25.310 --> 01:17:29.260
You find this kind in all the saloons
in all your prosperous communities!

884
01:17:29.530 --> 01:17:30.600
Wichita!

885
01:17:33.740 --> 01:17:35.730
Over in Cheyenne!

886
01:17:38.950 --> 01:17:40.200
Abilene!

887
01:17:44.040 --> 01:17:46.450
But you won't find them
in the town of Big Whiskey.

888
01:17:51.340 --> 01:17:54.050
Hurry up!
You know what to say to Little Bill.

889
01:17:54.300 --> 01:17:58.130
Now you guys look sharp for that lone pine.
You miss the pine, you ain't gonna find it.

890
01:17:58.390 --> 01:18:00.510
O.K. never mind the shirt, ma'am!
Put the fuck his boots on!

891
01:18:10.820 --> 01:18:13.490
What about Will?
What are we gonna do about Will?

892
01:18:13.520 --> 01:18:14.490
Come on, Kid!

893
01:18:14.660 --> 01:18:16.580
Let's hope them horses are still there!

894
01:18:51.280 --> 01:18:53.400
Let the man out, W.W.

895
01:18:54.160 --> 01:18:58.240
He's desiring to leave the hospitality
of Big Whiskey behind him.

896
01:19:31.620 --> 01:19:32.730
Easy Little Bill!
She's gotta work.

897
01:19:32.990 --> 01:19:34.990
She's got to turn a dollar a time.

898
01:19:35.190 --> 01:19:37.690
If they was just here for the fuckin'
how come they lit out the back window?

899
01:19:37.790 --> 01:19:40.280
On account of they seen you was
beating on their friend.

900
01:19:41.290 --> 01:19:43.380
They just come for the
billiards Little Bill, honest.

901
01:19:43.590 --> 01:19:44.380
Billiards?!

902
01:19:46.550 --> 01:19:48.460
What, you mean they were
just passing through here?

903
01:19:48.650 --> 01:19:50.460
They was going to Fort Buford.

904
01:19:50.720 --> 01:19:53.640
You just kicked the shit
out of an innocent man.

905
01:19:54.310 --> 01:19:55.590
Innocent?

906
01:19:55.940 --> 01:19:57.260
Innocent of what?

907
01:20:24.640 --> 01:20:26.160
Jesus, Ned!

908
01:20:26.640 --> 01:20:28.460
You done this before?

909
01:20:29.720 --> 01:20:31.220
Plenty times.

910
01:20:32.930 --> 01:20:35.090
His pistol must've jammed.

911
01:20:37.480 --> 01:20:41.100
Here.  Bring that candle in
a little closer.  I can't see.

912
01:20:52.660 --> 01:20:55.450
He wouldn't've take no beating
like that if it hadn't've jammed.

913
01:20:56.840 --> 01:20:59.460
He wouldn't just give it
over and not shoot no one.

914
01:21:03.550 --> 01:21:05.260
He don't look so good.

915
01:21:07.470 --> 01:21:09.260
He didn't even pull his pistol, huh?

916
01:21:09.520 --> 01:21:11.260
Yeah, well, he ain't
as tough as you, Kid.

917
01:21:11.320 --> 01:21:13.260
Yeah, well, at least I
would've pulled my pistol, Ned.

918
01:21:13.520 --> 01:21:16.520
You did!  Right out of the lady
and out the goddamn window!

919
01:21:16.770 --> 01:21:19.770
- That was your idea!  I wanted to go back--
- We got to go.

920
01:21:20.110 --> 01:21:23.150
What?  Already?  Hey, darlin' I'm
near ready for another advance.

921
01:21:23.410 --> 01:21:25.290
You're gonna use it all up
before you even get it.

922
01:21:25.400 --> 01:21:26.990
No more advances on
what you ain't done yet.

923
01:21:27.240 --> 01:21:30.070
Hey sweetheart, we're just waiting
on the weather to clear!

924
01:21:30.110 --> 01:21:31.870
Once this weather clears up...

925
01:21:31.920 --> 01:21:35.840
We're going to need more food!
About three days' worth.

926
01:21:36.290 --> 01:21:37.700
Three days?

927
01:21:38.710 --> 01:21:40.340
Ned, we could kill 'em tomorrow.

928
01:21:40.590 --> 01:21:42.420
I don't kill nobody without him.

929
01:21:42.590 --> 01:21:44.720
We don't need him!
The two of us could do it.

930
01:21:44.970 --> 01:21:46.300
Besides...

931
01:21:46.640 --> 01:21:49.470
...he ain't nothing
but a broken-down pig farmer.

932
01:21:50.060 --> 01:21:51.560
One of us'll bring
food in the morning.

933
01:21:51.660 --> 01:21:53.260
We'll bring you some whiskey too!

934
01:21:53.520 --> 01:21:55.680
And some medicine if you got any!

935
01:21:57.280 --> 01:21:59.650
Don't it make you sick
hearing him like that?

936
01:21:59.900 --> 01:22:01.530
Hey, don't you ladies worry none!

937
01:22:02.780 --> 01:22:06.150
Me and Ned, we'll kill them two
sons of bitches for ya!

938
01:22:13.130 --> 01:22:14.540
Claudia.

939
01:22:20.430 --> 01:22:23.040
Will?...  Will?

940
01:22:23.350 --> 01:22:24.980
Claudia's not here.

941
01:22:25.050 --> 01:22:26.380
Is that you, Ned?

942
01:22:28.310 --> 01:22:29.690
I seen him, Ned.

943
01:22:32.810 --> 01:22:35.020
I seen the Angel of Death.

944
01:22:35.650 --> 01:22:38.140
I seen a river, Ned.

945
01:22:39.110 --> 01:22:40.360
He's got snake eyes.

946
01:22:40.510 --> 01:22:43.360
Who Will?
Who's got snake eyes?

947
01:22:43.830 --> 01:22:45.650
It's the Angel of Death.

948
01:22:47.400 --> 01:22:49.030
Oh, Ned!

949
01:22:50.000 --> 01:22:51.830
I'm scared of dying.

950
01:22:52.500 --> 01:22:54.250
Easy, partner.  Easy.

951
01:22:54.880 --> 01:22:56.750
I seen Claudia too.

952
01:22:57.630 --> 01:23:00.880
That's good, Will!
That's good you saw Claudia, ain't it?

953
01:23:01.390 --> 01:23:03.880
Her face was all covered with worms.

954
01:23:04.850 --> 01:23:06.430
Oh Ned, I'm scared.

955
01:23:07.690 --> 01:23:09.100
I'm dying.

956
01:23:14.320 --> 01:23:16.110
No, don't tell nobody.

957
01:23:16.570 --> 01:23:18.480
Don't tell my kids...

958
01:23:19.070 --> 01:23:21.650
...none of the things I done.
You hear me?

959
01:23:23.660 --> 01:23:25.040
All right, Will.

960
01:23:42.430 --> 01:23:44.310
He's gonna die, ain't he?

961
01:23:45.810 --> 01:23:47.190
Maybe.

962
01:23:47.610 --> 01:23:49.760
Well, supposing he does?

963
01:23:53.570 --> 01:23:54.940
We'll bury him.

964
01:23:55.240 --> 01:23:57.060
That ain't what I mean, Ned.

965
01:24:00.790 --> 01:24:03.320
You mean will I help
you kill them cowboys?

966
01:24:05.420 --> 01:24:07.460
I can't spot them myself.

967
01:24:07.920 --> 01:24:09.410
But you could.

968
01:24:10.000 --> 01:24:14.130
That big bastard, you could spot him
a half-mile off, I bet.

969
01:24:15.590 --> 01:24:17.220
And if I spot him?

970
01:24:18.470 --> 01:24:20.960
Well then I ride up close and shoot him.

971
01:24:23.940 --> 01:24:25.180
Just like that?

972
01:24:25.650 --> 01:24:28.220
I told ya, I'm a damn killer.
I done it before.

973
01:24:31.280 --> 01:24:33.480
I'm more of a killer
than he is anyhow.

974
01:24:35.660 --> 01:24:36.800
Yeah?

975
01:24:39.060 --> 01:24:40.200
Yeah.

976
01:25:03.270 --> 01:25:05.060
I thought you was an angel.

977
01:25:07.230 --> 01:25:08.780
You ain't dead.

978
01:25:17.120 --> 01:25:18.700
Some big fellow he...

979
01:25:19.830 --> 01:25:21.910
...he really kicked the hell out of me.

980
01:25:24.790 --> 01:25:27.040
I must look kinda like you now.

981
01:25:29.130 --> 01:25:31.370
You don't look nothing like me, mister.

982
01:25:33.300 --> 01:25:34.930
No offense meant.

983
01:25:37.770 --> 01:25:40.390
You got to be the one
those cowboys cut up.

984
01:25:47.190 --> 01:25:49.770
My partners, Ned and that Kid...

985
01:25:50.320 --> 01:25:51.270
...they around?

986
01:25:52.830 --> 01:25:55.910
They went out scouting when
they saw your fever broke.

987
01:25:56.870 --> 01:25:57.950
Scouting?

988
01:25:58.870 --> 01:26:00.780
Out to the Bar T...

989
01:26:01.170 --> 01:26:03.080
...looking for them.

990
01:26:07.170 --> 01:26:08.970
How long I been here?

991
01:26:10.180 --> 01:26:11.590
Three days.

992
01:26:13.180 --> 01:26:14.800
Are you hungry or...

993
01:26:15.520 --> 01:26:17.310
Three days?

994
01:26:17.560 --> 01:26:19.100
I ought to be...

995
01:26:31.410 --> 01:26:33.780
I thought I was gone.

996
01:26:36.370 --> 01:26:40.500
I wouldn't normally pay no notice
to high country like this...

997
01:26:41.340 --> 01:26:43.870
...trees,
but I'm sure noticing now.

998
01:26:44.880 --> 01:26:47.370
I thought I was dying for sure.

999
01:26:49.220 --> 01:26:50.840
I brought your hat.

1000
01:26:51.180 --> 01:26:53.750
You left it down at Greely's.

1001
01:26:54.430 --> 01:26:55.710
Thanks.

1002
01:26:57.600 --> 01:26:58.980
That sheriff...

1003
01:27:00.230 --> 01:27:02.980
- He still looking for me?
- Little Bill?

1004
01:27:03.240 --> 01:27:05.990
No, he thinks you went South.

1005
01:27:09.240 --> 01:27:12.110
Are you really going
to kill them cowboys?

1006
01:27:13.250 --> 01:27:14.530
I guess.

1007
01:27:15.370 --> 01:27:17.830
Still a payment coming, isn't there?

1008
01:27:19.420 --> 01:27:22.170
Them other two, your friends...

1009
01:27:22.720 --> 01:27:25.800
...they been taking
advances on the payment.

1010
01:27:26.590 --> 01:27:28.000
Advances?

1011
01:27:29.970 --> 01:27:31.520
Free ones.

1012
01:27:31.970 --> 01:27:33.420
Free ones?

1013
01:27:33.980 --> 01:27:36.850
Alice and Silky been
giving them free ones.

1014
01:27:38.570 --> 01:27:40.020
Hmm, I see.

1015
01:27:43.780 --> 01:27:45.860
Would you like a free one?

1016
01:27:55.430 --> 01:27:57.410
No I... I guess not.

1017
01:27:58.210 --> 01:28:01.880
I didn't mean with me.
I meant...

1018
01:28:02.130 --> 01:28:06.680
...Alice and Silky would be happy
to give you a free one if you wanted one.

1019
01:28:07.010 --> 01:28:09.220
That's all I meant.

1020
01:28:10.600 --> 01:28:13.010
I didn't mean I...

1021
01:28:13.270 --> 01:28:17.350
...I didn't want a free one on
account of you been cut up and all.

1022
01:28:18.320 --> 01:28:21.940
What I said the other day about
you looking like me, that ain't true.

1023
01:28:22.660 --> 01:28:24.530
You ain't ugly like me.

1024
01:28:25.950 --> 01:28:29.450
It's just that we both got scars.

1025
01:28:31.620 --> 01:28:35.120
But you're a beautiful woman
and if I was to want a free one...

1026
01:28:35.300 --> 01:28:39.040
...I'd want it with you I
guess more than them other two.

1027
01:28:41.380 --> 01:28:42.760
It's just that I...

1028
01:28:43.510 --> 01:28:45.920
...I can't on account of my wife.

1029
01:28:52.520 --> 01:28:53.770
Your wife?

1030
01:28:54.420 --> 01:28:56.770
Yeah...  you see...

1031
01:29:02.910 --> 01:29:04.700
I admire you for that.

1032
01:29:05.410 --> 01:29:07.820
For being true to your wife and all.

1033
01:29:08.870 --> 01:29:11.000
I've known a lot of men...

1034
01:29:13.250 --> 01:29:14.660
...who weren't.

1035
01:29:16.950 --> 01:29:18.810
Yeah, I suppose.

1036
01:29:25.020 --> 01:29:26.810
Is she back in Kansas?

1037
01:29:28.730 --> 01:29:29.970
Yeah.

1038
01:29:31.020 --> 01:29:33.690
Yeah, she's watching over my young ones.

1039
01:29:38.780 --> 01:29:39.890
Hang on Slim!  Hang on.

1040
01:29:40.160 --> 01:29:42.030
Get the damn iron!  Hold it!

1041
01:29:42.960 --> 01:29:46.030
Davey!  Come on Davey-boy!
Come on Davey!

1042
01:29:51.840 --> 01:29:53.630
Jesus, fella!

1043
01:30:05.560 --> 01:30:07.720
Jesus, boys, my leg's broke!

1044
01:30:09.770 --> 01:30:11.350
I'm pinned, boys!

1045
01:30:12.780 --> 01:30:14.400
Better finish him, Ned.

1046
01:30:14.820 --> 01:30:16.980
He ain't dead?  You didn't get him?

1047
01:30:17.240 --> 01:30:19.150
He got the boy's horse.

1048
01:30:19.830 --> 01:30:22.200
Better finish him before he gets clear.

1049
01:30:25.000 --> 01:30:26.870
Get behind them rocks, Davey-boy.

1050
01:30:27.330 --> 01:30:28.910
Get over there, Davey!

1051
01:30:32.170 --> 01:30:34.920
What happened?
He ain't killed?!

1052
01:30:35.470 --> 01:30:36.420
What's going on?

1053
01:30:36.800 --> 01:30:39.260
He gets in those rocks,
we ain't gonna get him.

1054
01:30:39.640 --> 01:30:42.090
- Unless we go down there.
- What rocks?

1055
01:30:42.480 --> 01:30:45.260
Why don't you shoot?
What's going on, Ned?

1056
01:30:49.930 --> 01:30:51.560
Well ain't you gonna shoot?!

1057
01:30:55.030 --> 01:30:56.560
Will?

1058
01:31:04.870 --> 01:31:07.250
I ain't very good with one of these.

1059
01:31:12.880 --> 01:31:15.290
Keep going, Davey!
The rocks!  Keep going!

1060
01:31:17.510 --> 01:31:18.840
Did you get him?

1061
01:31:19.680 --> 01:31:20.930
Will, where is he?

1062
01:31:21.230 --> 01:31:23.430
How many more shots do I have?

1063
01:31:25.400 --> 01:31:28.270
Ned, goddamn it!
How many more shots do I have?

1064
01:31:31.360 --> 01:31:32.390
Two.

1065
01:31:44.670 --> 01:31:46.130
Did you get him?

1066
01:32:03.440 --> 01:32:05.350
Here, reload this.

1067
01:32:06.570 --> 01:32:08.850
- You missed him.
- I got him.

1068
01:32:12.910 --> 01:32:14.190
He ain't killed.

1069
01:32:14.910 --> 01:32:16.650
Maybe, maybe not.

1070
01:32:17.290 --> 01:32:19.360
Got him through the gut, I think.

1071
01:32:23.920 --> 01:32:25.540
You think he's gonna die?

1072
01:32:27.970 --> 01:32:29.210
You think we killed him?

1073
01:32:37.350 --> 01:32:38.730
Yeah.

1074
01:32:39.980 --> 01:32:43.310
We killed him, I guess.

1075
01:32:46.940 --> 01:32:48.850
I'm dying, boys!

1076
01:32:49.570 --> 01:32:53.070
Well then you shouldn't have
cut up no woman, you asshole!

1077
01:32:58.830 --> 01:33:01.500
Jesus, I'm so thirsty!

1078
01:33:02.210 --> 01:33:03.550
Slim!

1079
01:33:04.210 --> 01:33:07.550
Slim, give me some water, please!

1080
01:33:07.970 --> 01:33:09.210
Please, Slim!

1081
01:33:10.470 --> 01:33:12.090
I'm bleeding, Slim!

1082
01:33:16.350 --> 01:33:19.060
Give him a drink of water,
goddamn it!

1083
01:33:23.190 --> 01:33:27.240
Will you give him a drink of water,
for Christ's sake!  We ain't gonna shoot!

1084
01:33:29.280 --> 01:33:30.610
You ain't gonna shoot?

1085
01:33:31.180 --> 01:33:32.310
No!

1086
01:33:34.700 --> 01:33:36.410
Hold on, Davey-boy!

1087
01:33:37.670 --> 01:33:39.120
Here I come now!

1088
01:33:45.680 --> 01:33:47.630
Don't shoot me, you bastards!

1089
01:33:49.320 --> 01:33:50.570
Davey!

1090
01:33:51.220 --> 01:33:52.470
Shit!

1091
01:33:59.720 --> 01:34:00.870
Davey!

1092
01:34:02.400 --> 01:34:03.980
They take him water?

1093
01:34:04.500 --> 01:34:05.680
Yeah.

1094
01:34:06.740 --> 01:34:08.980
Jesus, Johnny!  They shot him!

1095
01:34:09.240 --> 01:34:10.820
Davey, hold on now!

1096
01:34:19.590 --> 01:34:23.120
You murdering bastards!
You killed our Davey-boy!

1097
01:34:32.060 --> 01:34:33.930
When we gonna double back?

1098
01:34:34.600 --> 01:34:36.350
After a ways.

1099
01:34:37.730 --> 01:34:38.980
Not me.

1100
01:34:39.780 --> 01:34:41.270
I'm heading on back down to Kansas.

1101
01:34:41.680 --> 01:34:44.270
We got to kill the other one first.

1102
01:34:45.280 --> 01:34:49.280
Look, Ned, with any luck, we'll find him
by nightfall or in the morning.

1103
01:34:49.540 --> 01:34:52.450
Then we can shoot him and
head on back with the money.

1104
01:34:54.580 --> 01:34:57.790
- You want the Spencer, Will?
- This ain't no time to quit, Ned.

1105
01:34:58.050 --> 01:35:00.500
- You know you're gonna lose your share Ned.
- Shut up!

1106
01:35:00.800 --> 01:35:03.500
I'll see you, Will.
So long, Kid.

1107
01:35:04.940 --> 01:35:06.210
Ned!

1108
01:35:11.340 --> 01:35:12.310
Here.

1109
01:35:12.940 --> 01:35:15.610
I ain't no good with that damn thing anyhow.

1110
01:35:16.110 --> 01:35:20.820
Look... me and the Kid'll head over
to that ranch and we find him we'll shoot him.

1111
01:35:21.280 --> 01:35:24.980
Then we'll meet up with you and pick up
our money and all head South together.

1112
01:35:25.780 --> 01:35:28.240
Well, supposing he don't go
back to the ranch, Will?

1113
01:35:28.620 --> 01:35:32.620
Well he ain't gonna go into town, I figure
he won't stay out in the open country.

1114
01:35:32.960 --> 01:35:34.920
No,  he'll hole up at that ranch.

1115
01:35:36.800 --> 01:35:38.250
Well I ain't waiting.

1116
01:35:38.800 --> 01:35:41.370
I'll look in on your
young ones when I get back.

1117
01:35:45.140 --> 01:35:46.330
Hey, Ned!

1118
01:35:48.140 --> 01:35:50.930
Don't pay no attention to what the
Kid said about the money and all.

1119
01:35:51.190 --> 01:35:52.430
I'll bring your share.

1120
01:35:56.690 --> 01:35:58.270
Kid's full of shit.

1121
01:36:16.980 --> 01:36:17.980
Little Bill?

1122
01:36:19.180 --> 01:36:20.180
Little Bill?

1123
01:36:26.480 --> 01:36:28.680
Just doing some repairs up here.

1124
01:36:29.060 --> 01:36:30.890
They killed one of them cowboys.

1125
01:36:34.990 --> 01:36:36.230
Shit!

1126
01:36:37.740 --> 01:36:42.280
Parsons said how he seen three men,
right after sunup, headed out East.

1127
01:36:42.540 --> 01:36:47.000
And one was on a dun and another
was on a flea-bitten grey.

1128
01:36:47.280 --> 01:36:49.530
Only he didn't know what
the third one was on,

1129
01:36:49.600 --> 01:36:51.830
could have been an Appaloosa 'cause
he was looking right into the sun.

1130
01:36:52.090 --> 01:36:56.170
Bill, Amos says to ask you if the county's
gonna pay for feed for all the horses or not.

1131
01:36:56.430 --> 01:36:59.710
Witherspoon says he won't sell us
no more 30-30 shells without we pay.

1132
01:36:59.970 --> 01:37:01.590
Hell, use my dogs!

1133
01:37:01.850 --> 01:37:04.090
Then the county's got to take responsibility.

1134
01:37:04.380 --> 01:37:06.520
Don't worry about them horses now...

1135
01:37:06.680 --> 01:37:09.520
you just get on out there to the Bar T
and make sure that other cowboy...

1136
01:37:09.770 --> 01:37:12.350
stays put and
don't expose himself, hear?

1137
01:37:22.370 --> 01:37:24.700
I didn't think they'd really do it.

1138
01:37:25.330 --> 01:37:28.200
Did you think they come clear
up from Kansas to fuck us?

1139
01:37:30.890 --> 01:37:34.960
No, but... that Kid, he's
just a boy and the other one...

1140
01:37:35.220 --> 01:37:38.090
...Will, the nice one, being
so true to his wife and all...

1141
01:37:38.350 --> 01:37:40.880
Wife?
He ain't got no wife.

1142
01:37:41.390 --> 01:37:44.230
- Oh yes, he does. He--
- I told ya, he ain't got no wife.

1143
01:37:44.730 --> 01:37:46.550
Not above ground, anyways.

1144
01:37:52.650 --> 01:37:54.060
Murdering whores!

1145
01:37:55.240 --> 01:37:56.730
He had it coming!

1146
01:37:57.080 --> 01:37:58.650
He had it coming for what he done.

1147
01:37:58.990 --> 01:38:00.320
And the other one too!

1148
01:38:00.580 --> 01:38:02.820
Both of them for what they done!

1149
01:38:13.010 --> 01:38:14.420
We got one!

1150
01:38:16.850 --> 01:38:19.520
We got one, Sheriff!
Out by Cow Creek!

1151
01:38:19.850 --> 01:38:22.220
- Is he alive?
- Hell, yeah!

1152
01:38:22.480 --> 01:38:27.100
Bunch of us boys from Bar T went out looking
on account of them killing one of our own.

1153
01:38:27.440 --> 01:38:30.610
Come across the son-of-a-bitch
on a roan heading South.

1154
01:38:30.950 --> 01:38:32.190
Did he admit it?

1155
01:38:32.530 --> 01:38:36.610
No.  But I guess he will soon enough.
Had a Spencer rifle on him.

1156
01:38:37.370 --> 01:38:38.860
Those cowboys messed him up?

1157
01:38:40.460 --> 01:38:41.950
A little bit I guess.

1158
01:38:43.830 --> 01:38:45.230
Alright.  Find Andy.

1159
01:38:45.630 --> 01:38:49.630
Get on out there.  See if you can find out
what happened to those other two fellas!

1160
01:39:12.740 --> 01:39:14.900
You see anything out there, Buck?

1161
01:39:15.160 --> 01:39:18.990
Hell, yes I did!
Seen about 200 fellas packing rifles.

1162
01:39:19.250 --> 01:39:23.540
Got the place surrounded.
Say they want Quick Mike's ass.

1163
01:39:23.790 --> 01:39:27.080
I said, "How much?"  They says,
"About five."  I said, "Dollars?"

1164
01:39:27.340 --> 01:39:28.590
They said, "Cents."

1165
01:39:28.840 --> 01:39:30.340
I said, "Sold."

1166
01:39:32.010 --> 01:39:33.670
Well, I ain't worried!

1167
01:39:34.010 --> 01:39:36.260
Because I got me some protection.

1168
01:40:02.040 --> 01:40:03.950
- Tell you where them others is?
- Nope.

1169
01:40:04.210 --> 01:40:05.290
Give 'em any names?

1170
01:40:05.630 --> 01:40:08.300
Didn't tell us nothing but
his own name, Ned Roundtree.

1171
01:40:10.890 --> 01:40:12.130
Bring him in.

1172
01:40:12.740 --> 01:40:14.080
Well Ned...

1173
01:40:15.140 --> 01:40:17.980
you'll want to tell me
and Mr. Beauchamp here...

1174
01:40:18.730 --> 01:40:20.970
all about your two
villainous friends I guess.

1175
01:40:21.610 --> 01:40:25.770
I'll be glad to hear the names and
whereabouts of those murderous son-of-a-bitches.

1176
01:40:40.630 --> 01:40:42.250
Sure is ripe.

1177
01:40:43.920 --> 01:40:45.750
Going to get a lot riper.

1178
01:40:47.180 --> 01:40:48.750
You think he's still in there?

1179
01:40:49.950 --> 01:40:51.590
Yeah, he's in there.

1180
01:40:52.850 --> 01:40:55.930
Yeah, well he's holding on to
his shit like it was money.

1181
01:40:56.850 --> 01:40:58.260
He's in there.

1182
01:40:58.770 --> 01:41:00.930
You tell me right off if you see him.

1183
01:41:01.360 --> 01:41:02.340
Yeah.

1184
01:41:03.360 --> 01:41:05.440
Ain't gonna shoot him
your own self, are you?

1185
01:41:05.950 --> 01:41:07.440
You can shoot him.

1186
01:41:45.280 --> 01:41:48.320
Now Ned... you and Mr. Quincy and...

1187
01:41:48.580 --> 01:41:50.520
What was the young fella's name?

1188
01:41:52.790 --> 01:41:53.670
Elroy...

1189
01:41:54.590 --> 01:41:56.370
Elroy Tate.

1190
01:42:01.260 --> 01:42:03.580
No... No, that's not what you said.

1191
01:42:04.050 --> 01:42:05.080
Hell if it ain't!

1192
01:42:05.430 --> 01:42:07.010
No, you said...

1193
01:42:07.600 --> 01:42:10.350
"Elroy Quincy out of Medicine Hat and...

1194
01:42:12.100 --> 01:42:14.850
Henry Tate out of Cheyenne."

1195
01:42:15.360 --> 01:42:16.770
Hell if I did.

1196
01:42:17.780 --> 01:42:19.190
Hell if I did.

1197
01:42:19.410 --> 01:42:20.740
Charley...

1198
01:42:21.410 --> 01:42:24.740
Go and get them whores what fucked
these boys the night of the storm.

1199
01:42:24.990 --> 01:42:27.030
Strawberry Alice and Silky?

1200
01:42:27.370 --> 01:42:29.030
Yeah!  Go on.  Get 'em!  Go on.

1201
01:42:35.090 --> 01:42:36.300
Now Ned...

1202
01:42:38.090 --> 01:42:42.300
Them whores are going to tell
different lies than you.

1203
01:42:43.550 --> 01:42:47.090
And when their lies
ain't the same as your lies...

1204
01:42:49.060 --> 01:42:51.270
well I ain't going to hurt no woman.

1205
01:42:52.400 --> 01:42:54.350
But I'm going to hurt you.

1206
01:42:56.820 --> 01:42:58.980
Not gentle like before...

1207
01:43:00.530 --> 01:43:01.860
...but bad.

1208
01:43:18.550 --> 01:43:19.800
Where you going?

1209
01:43:20.090 --> 01:43:22.340
- Goin out to the shithouse.
- Well let me finish this hand will ya?

1210
01:43:22.600 --> 01:43:24.840
What are you gonna protect
me while I take a dump?

1211
01:43:25.100 --> 01:43:27.260
- You're gonna get bushwhacked.
- I'll fart on them.

1212
01:43:27.520 --> 01:43:30.690
- I'll go with ya.
- Yeah, you can wipe my ass, Thirsty.

1213
01:43:30.940 --> 01:43:34.220
Hell with him, you know.
The man ain't polite, he oughta get shot.

1214
01:43:38.280 --> 01:43:39.610
Is that him?

1215
01:43:39.870 --> 01:43:41.360
Yeah, that's him.

1216
01:43:45.290 --> 01:43:48.120
All right, Kid.  Go get him.
He's all yours.

1217
01:44:24.670 --> 01:44:25.780
Assassins!

1218
01:44:29.710 --> 01:44:31.040
Shoot him!

1219
01:44:46.810 --> 01:44:48.360
Come on, goddamn it!

1220
01:45:05.460 --> 01:45:06.870
Did you get him?

1221
01:45:07.160 --> 01:45:08.470
Yeah.

1222
01:45:19.430 --> 01:45:20.710
Cover me.

1223
01:45:23.400 --> 01:45:25.770
- I can't see 'em!
- Just shoot damn ya!

1224
01:46:02.860 --> 01:46:05.430
Was that what it was like in
the old days Will?

1225
01:46:06.110 --> 01:46:08.650
Everybody riding out, shooting...

1226
01:46:09.110 --> 01:46:13.030
...smoke all over the place, folks
yelling, bullets whizzing by?

1227
01:46:14.870 --> 01:46:16.200
I guess so.

1228
01:46:20.290 --> 01:46:22.780
Shit, I thought they's gonna get us.

1229
01:46:23.960 --> 01:46:25.950
I was even scared a little.

1230
01:46:26.300 --> 01:46:27.540
Just for a minute.

1231
01:46:30.300 --> 01:46:32.290
Was you ever scared in them days?

1232
01:46:34.560 --> 01:46:35.970
I can't remember.

1233
01:46:37.310 --> 01:46:39.470
I was drunk most of the time.

1234
01:46:46.240 --> 01:46:48.810
I shot that fucker three times!

1235
01:46:50.320 --> 01:46:53.860
He was taking a shit, he went
for his pistol and I blazed away.

1236
01:46:54.410 --> 01:46:55.790
First shot...

1237
01:46:57.580 --> 01:46:59.240
...I got him right in the chest.

1238
01:47:03.380 --> 01:47:04.740
Say, Will.

1239
01:47:05.680 --> 01:47:06.640
Yeah?

1240
01:47:09.010 --> 01:47:10.470
That was the first one.

1241
01:47:12.010 --> 01:47:13.460
First one what?

1242
01:47:15.770 --> 01:47:17.590
First one I ever killed.

1243
01:47:19.150 --> 01:47:20.230
Yeah?

1244
01:47:21.610 --> 01:47:24.020
You know how I said I shot five men?

1245
01:47:25.450 --> 01:47:27.020
It weren't true.

1246
01:47:29.450 --> 01:47:31.610
That Mexican who come at me
with the knife?

1247
01:47:32.950 --> 01:47:37.370
I just busted his leg with a shovel.
I didn't kill him or nothing neither.

1248
01:47:40.590 --> 01:47:43.790
Well you sure killed the
hell out of that fellow today.

1249
01:47:45.760 --> 01:47:47.340
Hell, yeah!

1250
01:47:50.810 --> 01:47:53.180
I killed the hell out of him, didn't I?

1251
01:47:54.060 --> 01:47:57.100
Three shots and he was taking a shit.

1252
01:48:03.650 --> 01:48:05.030
Take a drink, Kid.

1253
01:48:15.920 --> 01:48:17.790
Jesus Christ!

1254
01:48:30.270 --> 01:48:32.140
It don't seem real.

1255
01:48:33.690 --> 01:48:36.810
How he ain't gonna never
breath again, ever.

1256
01:48:37.780 --> 01:48:39.100
How he's dead.

1257
01:48:40.950 --> 01:48:42.440
And the other one too.

1258
01:48:45.330 --> 01:48:47.570
All on account of pullin' a trigger.

1259
01:48:50.540 --> 01:48:53.180
It's a hell of a thing, killin' a man.

1260
01:48:54.940 --> 01:48:56.880
You take away all he's got...

1261
01:48:57.850 --> 01:49:00.060
...and all he's ever gonna have.

1262
01:49:03.220 --> 01:49:04.310
Yeah.

1263
01:49:05.720 --> 01:49:07.710
Well I guess they had it coming.

1264
01:49:13.730 --> 01:49:15.970
We all have it coming, Kid.

1265
01:49:30.580 --> 01:49:33.500
I was watching ya, seeing
that you weren't followed.

1266
01:49:34.920 --> 01:49:39.380
Silky and Faith they rode off to the East
and two deputies was following them.

1267
01:49:44.350 --> 01:49:47.280
Here... You wanna help me
count this stuff Kid?

1268
01:49:47.500 --> 01:49:49.480
I trust you Will.

1269
01:49:49.650 --> 01:49:52.250
Well don't go trusting me too much.

1270
01:49:52.940 --> 01:49:56.370
In fact, we'll give Ned
his share together.

1271
01:49:56.530 --> 01:49:59.150
That way you'll know I ain't
holding out on you.

1272
01:49:59.410 --> 01:50:00.650
Ned's share?

1273
01:50:02.540 --> 01:50:05.780
Yeah.  He went South.
We'll catch up to him.

1274
01:50:06.540 --> 01:50:08.330
Ned... He's dead.

1275
01:50:11.710 --> 01:50:13.340
What do you mean, he's dead?

1276
01:50:14.380 --> 01:50:17.250
He went South yesterday.
He ain't dead.

1277
01:50:17.800 --> 01:50:20.370
They...they killed him.
I...I thought you knew that.

1278
01:50:20.640 --> 01:50:22.550
Nobody killed Ned!

1279
01:50:22.810 --> 01:50:25.300
He didn't kill anyone.
He went South yesterday!

1280
01:50:25.680 --> 01:50:27.760
Why would anybody kill Ned?

1281
01:50:30.360 --> 01:50:31.600
Who killed him?

1282
01:50:32.400 --> 01:50:33.650
Li...Little Bill.

1283
01:50:33.990 --> 01:50:36.080
The Bar T boys caught him...

1284
01:50:36.150 --> 01:50:38.780
...and Little Bill...
he beat him up.

1285
01:50:39.030 --> 01:50:43.860
He was making him answer questions,
and beating him up and then Ned just died.

1286
01:50:44.330 --> 01:50:46.790
They got a sign on him
says he was a killer.

1287
01:50:47.040 --> 01:50:48.500
They got a sign on him?

1288
01:50:49.250 --> 01:50:50.830
In front of Greely's.

1289
01:50:51.090 --> 01:50:53.250
A sign on him in front of Greely's!

1290
01:50:57.840 --> 01:51:00.170
These questions Little Bill was asking...

1291
01:51:01.310 --> 01:51:02.680
...what kind were they?

1292
01:51:06.900 --> 01:51:09.690
About where you and him was.

1293
01:51:10.110 --> 01:51:11.350
Then what?

1294
01:51:12.440 --> 01:51:16.770
A cowboy come in saying you killed
Quick Mike in the shithouse at the Bar T.

1295
01:51:17.780 --> 01:51:20.650
So Little Bill killed him
for what we done, huh?

1296
01:51:20.810 --> 01:51:22.260
Not on purpose.

1297
01:51:23.210 --> 01:51:25.200
But he started hurting him worse.

1298
01:51:25.460 --> 01:51:27.200
Making him tell stuff.

1299
01:51:27.540 --> 01:51:29.150
First, Ned wouldn't say nothing.

1300
01:51:29.880 --> 01:51:33.630
...and then Little Bill hurt him
so bad, he said who you was.

1301
01:51:35.720 --> 01:51:39.140
He said how you was really
William Munny out of Missouri.

1302
01:51:39.970 --> 01:51:43.010
...and Little Bill said, "The same
William Munny that dynamited the

1303
01:51:43.270 --> 01:51:46.470
...Rock Island & Pacific in '69,
killing women and children and all?"

1304
01:51:46.730 --> 01:51:49.900
...and Ned said you done a lot worse
than that.  Said you was...

1305
01:51:50.150 --> 01:51:53.820
...more cold-blooded than William Bonney
and how if he hurt Ned again...

1306
01:51:54.070 --> 01:51:59.230
...you was gonna come kill him
like you killed the U.S. Marshal in '70.

1307
01:52:03.920 --> 01:52:06.080
That didn't scare Little Bill, did it?

1308
01:52:08.090 --> 01:52:09.330
No, sir.

1309
01:52:17.350 --> 01:52:19.170
Give me your Schofield.

1310
01:52:19.430 --> 01:52:20.630
What for Will?

1311
01:52:20.890 --> 01:52:21.890
Give it to me.

1312
01:52:23.090 --> 01:52:24.690
Yeah.  Sure.

1313
01:52:29.160 --> 01:52:31.150
You go on, keep it.

1314
01:52:31.410 --> 01:52:33.080
I'm never gonna use it again.

1315
01:52:35.370 --> 01:52:37.440
I won't kill nobody no more.

1316
01:52:41.040 --> 01:52:42.670
I ain't like you, Will.

1317
01:52:46.710 --> 01:52:48.620
You better ride on back, Miss.

1318
01:52:53.390 --> 01:52:55.960
Go on, keep it...all of it.
It's yours.

1319
01:52:56.850 --> 01:52:59.720
What about the spectacles
and the fancy clothes?

1320
01:53:00.810 --> 01:53:04.010
I guess I'd rather be blind
and ragged than dead.

1321
01:53:05.090 --> 01:53:09.240
You don't have to worry, Kid.
I ain't going to kill you.

1322
01:53:09.660 --> 01:53:11.730
You're the only friend I got.

1323
01:53:19.170 --> 01:53:24.210
Here, take this money and give my half
and Ned's half to my kids.

1324
01:53:24.800 --> 01:53:28.330
Tell them if I ain't back in a week,
they give half to Sally Two Trees.

1325
01:53:28.590 --> 01:53:31.300
You can keep the rest.
You can get them spectacles now.

1326
01:53:31.550 --> 01:53:33.300
You're gonna kill Little Bill aint ya?

1327
01:53:33.770 --> 01:53:37.850
You stay clear of folks you see.
There'll be a lot of 'em out to hang you.

1328
01:53:38.440 --> 01:53:39.720
Get going.

1329
01:54:23.530 --> 01:54:27.360
Alright I'm gonna say this just one more time,
to make it clear, so don't ask me again!

1330
01:54:27.950 --> 01:54:32.240
Those of you on the posse today got one
drink coming from the county budget!

1331
01:54:34.580 --> 01:54:37.870
And those of you who rode yesterday
get one drink for that too.

1332
01:54:39.170 --> 01:54:40.710
Alright hold it!  Now hold it.

1333
01:54:40.960 --> 01:54:45.420
Now that's two!  But after that, it comes out
of your own pocket!  Do you hear me Skinny?

1334
01:54:45.680 --> 01:54:48.710
- Yes, sir.
- Alright, we're pulling out early in the morning.

1335
01:54:49.140 --> 01:54:53.520
We're gonna chase these fellas clear down to Texas,
so don't spend too much of your own money.

1336
01:54:54.480 --> 01:54:57.100
We're gonna divide up into four parties!

1337
01:54:57.360 --> 01:54:59.640
...and we'll hit all the
farms and the trails...

1338
01:54:59.900 --> 01:55:01.310
...to make a big circle...

1339
01:55:01.570 --> 01:55:03.480
...and we're bound to come across somebody...

1340
01:55:03.740 --> 01:55:05.810
...that's seen these... skunks.

1341
01:55:23.340 --> 01:55:25.500
Who's the fella owns this shithole?

1342
01:55:35.110 --> 01:55:38.480
You, fat man.  Speak up.

1343
01:55:41.110 --> 01:55:43.570
I own this establishment.

1344
01:55:46.030 --> 01:55:49.700
I bought it from Greely for $1,000.

1345
01:55:51.120 --> 01:55:52.750
You better clear outta there.

1346
01:55:55.380 --> 01:55:58.260
Just hold it right there.
Hold it!

1347
01:56:07.890 --> 01:56:10.980
Well sir, you are
a cowardly son-of-a-bitch!

1348
01:56:12.190 --> 01:56:13.930
You just shot an unarmed man.

1349
01:56:14.400 --> 01:56:16.440
Well he should've armed himself...

1350
01:56:16.690 --> 01:56:19.440
...if he's gonna decorate his
saloon with my friend.

1351
01:56:20.160 --> 01:56:22.820
You'd be William Munny
out of Missouri...

1352
01:56:23.280 --> 01:56:25.160
...killer of women and children.

1353
01:56:25.830 --> 01:56:27.240
That's right.

1354
01:56:28.960 --> 01:56:30.910
I've killed women and children.

1355
01:56:32.460 --> 01:56:36.330
Killed just about everything that
walks or crawls at one time or another.

1356
01:56:37.590 --> 01:56:40.460
And I'm here to kill you, Little Bill.

1357
01:56:41.100 --> 01:56:43.420
For what you did to Ned.

1358
01:56:47.600 --> 01:56:49.510
You boys better move away.

1359
01:56:59.990 --> 01:57:04.150
All right, gentlemen.
He's got one barrel left.

1360
01:57:04.740 --> 01:57:07.400
When he fires that,
take out your pistols...

1361
01:57:07.660 --> 01:57:11.040
...and shoot him down
like the mangy scoundrel he is!

1362
01:57:24.610 --> 01:57:27.760
Misfire!  Kill the son-of-a-bitch!

1363
01:58:04.100 --> 01:58:08.450
Any man don't want to get killed,
better clear on out the back.

1364
01:58:52.910 --> 01:58:54.570
I'm shot!  I'm shot!

1365
01:58:55.070 --> 01:58:56.400
You ain't shot.

1366
01:58:58.660 --> 01:58:59.810
Oh, look, please...

1367
01:59:02.460 --> 01:59:05.410
I don't have a gun.
I am not armed.

1368
01:59:06.840 --> 01:59:08.330
Pick up that rifle.

1369
01:59:10.300 --> 01:59:11.580
Pick it up.

1370
01:59:13.970 --> 01:59:15.050
Shells too.

1371
01:59:28.280 --> 01:59:29.740
You killed Little Bill.

1372
01:59:31.280 --> 01:59:32.780
Sure you ain't armed?

1373
01:59:35.200 --> 01:59:37.110
No... look...I'm not.
I don't have a gun.

1374
01:59:37.370 --> 01:59:40.080
I've never had a gun.
I write.  I'm a writer!

1375
01:59:41.540 --> 01:59:43.040
A writer?

1376
01:59:43.840 --> 01:59:45.960
- What, letters and such?
- No, books.

1377
01:59:46.670 --> 01:59:47.750
Books.

1378
01:59:48.380 --> 01:59:52.300
I don't believe it, you killed five men.
Single-handed.

1379
01:59:54.380 --> 01:59:55.600
Yeah.

1380
02:00:00.900 --> 02:00:03.100
That's a Spencer rifle, right?

1381
02:00:03.380 --> 02:00:04.400
That's right.

1382
02:00:11.530 --> 02:00:13.440
Who a... who'd you kill first?

1383
02:00:14.730 --> 02:00:15.340
Huh?

1384
02:00:17.370 --> 02:00:19.620
"When confronted by superior numbers...

1385
02:00:19.780 --> 02:00:22.900
...an experienced gunfighter will
always fire on the best shot first."

1386
02:00:23.280 --> 02:00:24.450
Is that so?

1387
02:00:24.580 --> 02:00:27.710
Yeah... Little Bill told me that.
You probably killed him first didn't ya?

1388
02:00:28.590 --> 02:00:30.630
I was lucky in the order.

1389
02:00:31.600 --> 02:00:34.430
But I've always been lucky
when it comes to killing folks.

1390
02:00:38.230 --> 02:00:40.220
Who was next?
...was Clyde, right?

1391
02:00:40.480 --> 02:00:43.190
You musta killed Clyde,
well coulda been Deputy Andy...

1392
02:00:43.440 --> 02:00:46.060
All I can tell you
is who's gonna be last.

1393
02:01:22.740 --> 02:01:24.690
I don't deserve this.

1394
02:01:26.740 --> 02:01:28.320
To die like this.

1395
02:01:31.160 --> 02:01:33.150
I was building a house.

1396
02:01:34.170 --> 02:01:36.830
Deserve's got nothing to do with it.

1397
02:01:39.550 --> 02:01:41.790
I'll see you in hell, William Munny.

1398
02:01:49.050 --> 02:01:50.390
Yeah.

1399
02:02:22.300 --> 02:02:24.420
All right, I'm coming out!

1400
02:02:24.850 --> 02:02:27.630
Any man I see out there,
I'm gonna kill him!

1401
02:02:28.220 --> 02:02:30.720
Any sumbitch takes a shot at me...

1402
02:02:31.440 --> 02:02:36.260
...I'm not only going to kill him, I'm
gonna kill his wife and all his friends...

1403
02:02:36.610 --> 02:02:38.850
...and burn his damn house down!

1404
02:02:46.200 --> 02:02:47.990
Nobody better shoot!

1405
02:03:03.550 --> 02:03:05.630
O.K. Charley Heckor, go ahead.
Shoot him!

1406
02:03:19.780 --> 02:03:21.110
I can't.

1407
02:03:21.570 --> 02:03:24.360
Hell, no!
I ain't no deputy!

1408
02:03:44.270 --> 02:03:46.890
You better bury Ned right!

1409
02:03:47.480 --> 02:03:51.180
You better not cut up
nor otherwise harm no whores!

1410
02:03:55.110 --> 02:03:58.530
Or I'll come back and kill every
one of you sons a bitches.
